{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/973545-the-hedge-not-the-supplement-book","id":973545,"title":"The Hedge: Not The Supplement Book","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-20T18:11:02-07:00","id":973545,"title":"The Hedge: Not The Supplement Book","content":"Hey, <br /> <br /> I just posted the section we've got on The Hedge. It's got some rules and stuff. And things. Also, changing your Seemings. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/changeling-the-lost-the-hedge/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://theonyxpath.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/11/OPP-Metal.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/changeling-the-lost-the-hedge/\" target=\"_blank\"> Changeling: The Lost, The Hedge &ndash; Onyx Path Publishing </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/changeling-the-lost-the-hedge/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://theonyxpath.com/changeling-the-lost-the-hedge/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T18:25:13-07:00","id":973550,"title":"","content":"It seems very interesting, thematic and makes me want to get to playing a game of Changeling, so fantastic job there. As I mentioned in a comment, I spotted a couple typos, the main one being the &quot;change lanes&quot; rather than changelings one. One thing I do wonder now though, is it possible the Hedge is a little too psycho-reactive. My impression was that previously the Hedge was only really responsive in the presence of high Wyrd or Mantle. The description of the Changeling who's father died on a hay hook changing the local brambles into steel seems like it would be very easy to read another changelings fears just by being near them in the hedge.<br /> <br /> Oh, and the link to the google text at the bottom of the post isn't a hotlink.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5439-gullinbursti","name":"Gullinbursti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5439_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"291"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T18:26:39-07:00","id":973551,"title":"","content":"Nice!<br /> Just... am I blind, or does this excerpt not mention the damage one takes from the thorns? (I assume the mental effects are those who get linked to clarity at page XX) The only mention of this is that the Gentry doesn't take any damage from it.<br /> <br /> Also, the hedge shaping, just to get it, that's in addition to the stuff one does in a Hollow bought with a Merit, yes?<br /> Speaking of Hollows; Can one work those hedge shaping actions within a Hollow?<br /> <br /> Edit: Oh, and I just wanted to say, that despite my questions, I loved this. This is great!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T18:27:35-07:00","id":973553,"title":"","content":"Let me see if I can fix that hot link. <br /> <br /> And don't worry, this hasn't all been through editing yet. It's still in development. <br /> <br /> The reason I opened up the psychoreactive bit was because I want it to respond to humans. I'm not saying it's because Labyrinth. But I'm not saying it's not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T18:28:56-07:00","id":973556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/973545-the-hedge-not-the-supplement-book?p=973551#post973551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nice!<br /> Just... am I blind, or does this excerpt not mention the damage one takes from the thorns? (I assume the mental effects are those who get linked to clarity at page XX) The only mention of this is that the Gentry doesn't take any damage from it.<br /> <br /> Also, the hedge shaping, just to get it, that's in addition to the stuff one does in a Hollow bought with a Merit, yes?<br /> Speaking of Hollows; Can one work those hedge shaping actions within a Hollow?<br /> <br /> Edit: Oh, and I just wanted to say, that despite my questions, I loved this. This is great!</div> </div> </div> </div>You're not blind. It's considered an Extreme Environment, usually rank 1-3. <br /> <br /> Hollows are their own thing. You make them through the same process. But this is just &quot;do anywhere&quot; warping. And yes, you could do all that within a Hollow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T18:29:44-07:00","id":973557,"title":"","content":"I don't know, with Labyrinth, if it was truly psychoreactive, well after meeting with the Goblin King, I think it'd have been a lot more phallic... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5439-gullinbursti","name":"Gullinbursti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5439_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"291"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T18:33:17-07:00","id":973559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/973545-the-hedge-not-the-supplement-book?p=973556#post973556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You're not blind. It's considered an Extreme Environment, usually rank 1-3.<br /> <br /> Hollows are their own thing. You make them through the same process. But this is just &quot;do anywhere&quot; warping. And yes, you could do all that within a Hollow.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, you could for instance justify buying a Hollow merit just by starting a hedge shaping in a place you like?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gullinbursti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/973545-the-hedge-not-the-supplement-book?p=973557#post973557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know, with Labyrinth, if it was truly psychoreactive, well after meeting with the Goblin King, I think it'd have been a lot more phallic... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Bulging, if nothing else...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T18:38:15-07:00","id":973561,"title":"","content":"Well, with the increased psychoreactivity (there I go, making up words... I hope). Would a mechanic such as Hedge Insight, be plausible. Some kind of Wits+Investigation+Wyrd of Target to gain an insight as to traumas/fears of the target. This could result in something like a tilt or condition which allows the person gaining the insight to have a bonus to intimidation against the targeted individual.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5439-gullinbursti","name":"Gullinbursti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5439_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"291"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T18:42:01-07:00","id":973563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gullinbursti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/973545-the-hedge-not-the-supplement-book?p=973561#post973561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, with the increased psychoreactivity (there I go, making up words... I hope). Would a mechanic such as Hedge Insight, be plausible. Some kind of Wits+Investigation+Wyrd of Target to gain an insight as to traumas/fears of the target. This could result in something like a tilt or condition which allows the person gaining the insight to have a bonus to intimidation against the targeted individual.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's really cool. Probably Wyrd or equivalent as well, since the Hedge reacts to that too. Not as directly as emotions, to be sure, but if one looks at deliberate shaping, and the faster travel times, the Hedge sure serves the powerful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T18:42:24-07:00","id":973565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/973545-the-hedge-not-the-supplement-book?p=973559#post973559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, you could for instance justify buying a Hollow merit just by starting a hedge shaping in a place you like?<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. That's one way you can get a Hollow. You just make one where there wasn't. It'd take a long time (not directly dictated by rules) because it requires exceptional successes. But, the implication would be it's easier for people with high Wyrd. <br /> <br /> Theoretically, humans could even make Hollows. Theoretically. But it'd be hard. And at what point do they start becoming hobgoblins?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T18:43:38-07:00","id":973566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gullinbursti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/973545-the-hedge-not-the-supplement-book?p=973561#post973561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, with the increased psychoreactivity (there I go, making up words... I hope). Would a mechanic such as Hedge Insight, be plausible. Some kind of Wits+Investigation+Wyrd of Target to gain an insight as to traumas/fears of the target. This could result in something like a tilt or condition which allows the person gaining the insight to have a bonus to intimidation against the targeted individual.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a cool idea. Gosh, that sounds like something that would make really great additional rules and story possibilities if we ever did a supplement about the Hedge.<br /> <br /> (Yes, this totally was a thing I wanted to expound upon later.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T18:46:18-07:00","id":973569,"title":"","content":"By growing and shrinking,<br /> by eating and drinking,<br /> By placing and timing,<br /> by dreaming and rhyming-<br /> These are the ways you walk<br /> through trauma and chill loch.<br /> Beware the Hedge, my dear,<br /> both sky and loam,<br /> There's not another tear<br /> for you, the lost.<br /> <br /> We're gonna have some <i>fun</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T18:54:59-07:00","id":973576,"title":"","content":"I need to read this in detail at a more reasonable hour, but I really like the presentation of psychoactive and symbolic nuance in the Hedge's workings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 09-20-2016, 10:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T19:26:09-07:00","id":973590,"title":"","content":"Awesome stuff, its very flavourful. It was fun reading it.<br /> <br /> I just have 2 concerns, one really minor.<br /> <br /> The minor one is you say goblin fruit can't grow outside the Hedge, yet that Bramble and Thorns contract, an exceptional success causes a goblin fruit to grow on your summoned thorns.<br /> <br /> The second thing is where the Dream Bastions, are they still a thing, or are they gone, with the Onierons dream creatures as well?<br /> <br /> Also does that mean Hedgewall Contract doesn't nessarily summon an actual hedge, like could it be &quot;thorns&quot; consisting of rusty nails and coat hangars, fake finger nails and broken tazor blades, or of bone and bone shards?<br /> <br /> And thank you for sharing this, my excitement builds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T19:29:37-07:00","id":973593,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/973545-the-hedge-not-the-supplement-book?p=973590#post973590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Awesome stuff, its very flavourful. It was fun reading it.<br /> <br /> I just have 2 concerns, one really minor.<br /> <br /> The minor one is you say goblin fruit can't grow outside the Hedge, yet that Bramble and Thorns contract, an exceptional success causes a goblin fruit to grow on your summoned thorns.<br /> <br /> The second thing is where the Dream Bastions, are they still a thing, or are they gone, with the Onierons dream creatures as well?<br /> <br /> Also does that mean Hedgewall Contract doesn't nessarily summon an actual hedge, like could it be &amp;quot;thorns&amp;quot; consisting of rusty nails and coat hangars, fake finger nails and broken tazor blades, or of bone and bone shards?<br /> <br /> And thank you for sharing this, my excitement builds.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, the Contract is a more specific rule than the Hedge section. So, it supersedes the general statement. It's a rare exception, and one that takes unique intervention. <br /> <br /> And Dream Bastions are a thing, and dream critters exist. They are in their own section dealing specifically with dreams stuff. <br /> <br /> And yes, Hedgewall should create &quot;Hedge&quot;, not necessarily thorns and brambles specifically. I think in the final version, I might even make it subject to warping.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T19:56:29-07:00","id":973602,"title":"","content":"So! I've been re-reading the hedge-shaping again, and have some more thoughts!<br /> What would be the target number of the hedge-shaping roll? Just the amount of points one wants to bring? If one wants to make stuff with modifiers, would that mean increased target number or penalty on the rolls?<br /> If one hedge-shapes within a Hollow, does things still fade at the same rate, or does the more stable nature of the Hollow mean it lasts for longer?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T20:03:06-07:00","id":973605,"title":"","content":"I have only skimmed through the draft, but I can safely say that this was worth the wait <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Not only are a lot of the mechanics simpler, but there's some new stuff added in that makes a number of story hooks possible. The &quot;Changing Seemings&quot; hook is especially interesting (and it makes me even more curious about what the book will have on Loyalists and Seeming-less Lost).<br /> <br /> Working out systems for the breaking points of other splats in the Hedge shouldn't be a problem, in my opinion. Especially if one has a copy of Equinox Road.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T20:11:41-07:00","id":973606,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/973545-the-hedge-not-the-supplement-book?p=973602#post973602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So! I've been re-reading the hedge-shaping again, and have some more thoughts!<br /> What would be the target number of the hedge-shaping roll? Just the amount of points one wants to bring? If one wants to make stuff with modifiers, would that mean increased target number or penalty on the rolls?<br /> If one hedge-shapes within a Hollow, does things still fade at the same rate, or does the more stable nature of the Hollow mean it lasts for longer?</div> </div> </div> </div>There's no real target. You just put in the successes you want. You could theoretically make more rolls if you want further modifications. <br /> <br /> And Hollows don't have an inherent, written-in rule that modifications last longer. I might change that though? But it'd be within constraints of the Merit. Like, your modifications last longer, and others' fade quicker.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T20:20:02-07:00","id":973608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/973545-the-hedge-not-the-supplement-book?p=973606#post973606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's no real target. You just put in the successes you want. You could theoretically make more rolls if you want further modifications.<br /> <br /> And Hollows don't have an inherent, written-in rule that modifications last longer. I might change that though? But it'd be within constraints of the Merit. Like, your modifications last longer, and others' fade quicker.</div> </div> </div> </div>With the targets: It says to apply penalty equal to the modifier you want to create. Does that mean you add that to the end goal in the extended roll?<br /> Overall, shouldn't all the effects really be penalty on instant, target on extended? It'd kind of fit with the soul of it all. Making it harder to create permanent things on the spur of the moment. As it looks right now, with no cost, and no penalty, there is no reason to do the extended action, you can just take the instant action over and over again until you have all the effects you want.<br /> <br /> Oh, also, could one use this system to create things like tools and weapons? And can one carry them off, or are they bound to the place of their creation, or somesuch?<br /> <br /> I really apologize for the amount of questions, but this interests me deeply!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T20:26:37-07:00","id":973610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/973545-the-hedge-not-the-supplement-book?p=973608#post973608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> With the targets: It says to apply penalty equal to the modifier you want to create. Does that mean you add that to the end goal in the extended roll?<br /> Overall, shouldn't all the effects really be penalty on instant, target on extended? It'd kind of fit with the soul of it all. Making it harder to create permanent things on the spur of the moment. As it looks right now, with no cost, and no penalty, there is no reason to do the extended action, you can just take the instant action over and over again until you have all the effects you want.<br /> <br /> Oh, also, could one use this system to create things like tools and weapons? And can one carry them off, or are they bound to the place of their creation, or somesuch?<br /> <br /> I really apologize for the amount of questions, but this interests me deeply!</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh no, you'd apply that to the dice pool. If you want a +3 tool, or a spike that causes 3 lethal when you impale someone on it, you take -3 to your roll. That COULD be an issue with extended actions if you plan to do a bunch of shit with one action. But, that kind of incentivizes you to compartmentalize your different desired reshapes. <br /> <br /> I'll try to work in a little reason to opt for extended over multiple instants. Basically, the idea would be, you can't really build on something made with an instant action. It's more or less what it is, until it fades. <br /> <br /> And yes, you can carry things made in the Hedge within the Hedge. Once outside, they'd rapidly decay.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T20:32:31-07:00","id":973612,"title":"","content":"Curious, say I create a pitchfork to fend off a scarecrow-like hobgoblin and then hightail it out of the hedge. How do you envision the decay occurring visually. Would the wood rot and metal rust away at an incredibly rapid rate, or would it revert back into bramble like vegetable material?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5439-gullinbursti","name":"Gullinbursti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5439_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"291"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T20:32:34-07:00","id":973613,"title":"","content":"I feel bad saying this, but this is everything I <i>didn't</i> want in 2e.<br /> <br /> The focus on pain... Why? What does that add? What value does it bring? Why actively discourage exploration when you can simply let strong emotions do as they naturally will? No-one needs to tell you how love can lead to fear, anxiety, or obsession; how joy and delight can quickly become retreat from responsibility; sorrow, frigid depression and immobility; fear, to paranoia. The Hedge doesn't need to define itself as pain; merely the extreme. It achieves the same effect, without the explicit caveat that there cannot be benefits to it; that no-one gets out without paying in blood.<br /> <br /> Changeling 1e had a big problem with this; with <i>everything</i> exacting a toll and the Lost never seeming to be able to get anything without making a gut-wrenching sacrifice. I don't <i>want</i> that. I want more carrot and less stick. The very fact that there are Hobs and the proximity to Arcadia alone should be enough to make the Hedge scary; it has <i>enough</i> stick. It doesn't need its entire thesis to be &quot;This place exists to hurt you and make you miserable&quot; on top of that. It's just a repeat of having far, far more terror than wonder in a game of terrible wonder.<br /> <br /> Why not make the Hedge into a metaphor for attachment? For the dangers of extremes? For an inability to let go of the wonder of Arcadia and, thus, willingly walk into Arcadia's clutches?<br /> <br /> Why make it simply a wall of agony?<br /> <br /> Why?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T20:39:01-07:00","id":973616,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/973545-the-hedge-not-the-supplement-book?p=973613#post973613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel bad saying this, but this is everything I <i>didn't</i> want in 2e.<br /> <br /> The focus on pain... Why? What does that add? What value does it bring? Why actively discourage exploration when you can simply let strong emotions do as they naturally will? No-one needs to tell you how love can lead to fear, anxiety, or obsession; how joy and delight can quickly become retreat from responsibility; sorrow, frigid depression and immobility; fear, to paranoia. The Hedge doesn't need to define itself as pain; merely the extreme. It achieves the same effect, without the explicit caveat that there cannot be benefits to it; that no-one gets out without paying in blood.<br /> <br /> Changeling 1e had a big problem with this; with <i>everything</i> exacting a toll and the Lost never seeming to be able to get anything without making a gut-wrenching sacrifice. I don't <i>want</i> that. I want more carrot and less stick. The very fact that there are Hobs and the proximity to Arcadia alone should be enough to make the Hedge scary; it has <i>enough</i> stick. It doesn't need its entire thesis to be &quot;This place exists to hurt you and make you miserable&quot; on top of that. It's just a repeat of having far, far more terror than wonder in a game of terrible wonder.<br /> <br /> Why not make the Hedge into a metaphor for attachment? For the dangers of extremes? For an inability to let go of the wonder of Arcadia and, thus, willingly walk into Arcadia's clutches?<br /> <br /> Why make it simply a wall of agony?<br /> <br /> Why?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because the True Fae need to fear the Hedge too, and if there is one thing they hate more than changelings can, it's pain.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T20:46:09-07:00","id":973621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/973545-the-hedge-not-the-supplement-book?p=973613#post973613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel bad saying this, but this is everything I <i>didn't</i> want in 2e.<br /> <br /> The focus on pain... Why? What does that add? What value does it bring? Why actively discourage exploration when you can simply let strong emotions do as they naturally will? No-one needs to tell you how love can lead to fear, anxiety, or obsession; how joy and delight can quickly become retreat from responsibility; sorrow, frigid depression and immobility; fear, to paranoia. The Hedge doesn't need to define itself as pain; merely the extreme. It achieves the same effect, without the explicit caveat that there cannot be benefits to it; that no-one gets out without paying in blood.<br /> <br /> Changeling 1e had a big problem with this; with <i>everything</i> exacting a toll and the Lost never seeming to be able to get anything without making a gut-wrenching sacrifice. I don't <i>want</i> that. I want more carrot and less stick. The very fact that there are Hobs and the proximity to Arcadia alone should be enough to make the Hedge scary; it has <i>enough</i> stick. It doesn't need its entire thesis to be &quot;This place exists to hurt you and make you miserable&quot; on top of that. It's just a repeat of having far, far more terror than wonder in a game of terrible wonder.<br /> <br /> Why not make the Hedge into a metaphor for attachment? For the dangers of extremes? For an inability to let go of the wonder of Arcadia and, thus, willingly walk into Arcadia's clutches?<br /> <br /> Why make it simply a wall of agony?<br /> <br /> Why?</div> </div> </div> </div>I... sort of agree. I want there to be pain and fear in the place. But yeah. There should be plenty of beauty and wonder as well. If that is cut, we lose something from the setting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/973545-the-hedge-not-the-supplement-book?p=973610#post973610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh no, you'd apply that to the dice pool. If you want a +3 tool, or a spike that causes 3 lethal when you impale someone on it, you take -3 to your roll. That COULD be an issue with extended actions if you plan to do a bunch of shit with one action. But, that kind of incentivizes you to compartmentalize your different desired reshapes.<br /> <br /> I'll try to work in a little reason to opt for extended over multiple instants. Basically, the idea would be, you can't really build on something made with an instant action. It's more or less what it is, until it fades.<br /> <br /> And yes, you can carry things made in the Hedge within the Hedge. Once outside, they'd rapidly decay.</div> </div> </div> </div>As long as there are reasons to use both I'm happy!<br /> <br /> So basically, the goal is: Instant action for tools and weapons. Extended for dedicated re-shaping?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T20:46:28-07:00","id":973622,"title":"","content":"That doesn't really address my complaint. There being a particular in-universe explanation for it doesn't make this any less of an un-fun feature of the game line; one that has managed to actually scare off people in my gaming group from playing Changeling, and me from wanting to use the game line.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T21:06:09-07:00","id":973632,"title":"","content":"Now feel free to educate me if I'm mistaken, but wouldn't Dreaming suit you better if you'd prefer a game more focused on the wonder of Arcadia over Lost's darker interpretation of Fae mythology? Not saying that to be snide, I don't know an excessive amount about Dreaming, but that's the impression that I get.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5439-gullinbursti","name":"Gullinbursti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5439_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"291"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T21:11:22-07:00","id":973634,"title":"","content":"I'm not that fond of the focus on negative emotions. The Hedge should be a dangerous place, but that doesn't mean that it should make value judgements. It's psychoreactive, and that should deal with much more than just pain. I mean, this is well written, and I like the imagery, but I don't like &quot;if something doesn't hurt, the Hedge stops embodying it&quot;. There should be joy and pleasure in the Hedge (and those should be just as dangerous). I mean, to use an example you already used, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar70_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"70\" data-vbnamecard=\"70\">MachineIV</a>, The Labyrinth wasn't all horror and anguish. In fact, there was quite a lot of beauty there, and Sarah ended up in the Labyrinth in the first place because she wished for it, and got everything she asked for. I mean, there's even <a href=\"https://youtu.be/VppuD1St8Ec\" target=\"_blank\">a whole musical number</a> about how the pretty beautiful wishfulfillment is <i>more</i> dangerous than the horrors and stench bogs.<br /> <br /> I'd rather see perverted joy run amok than simply all pain all the time as if it were Silent Hill. The House of Crimson Indulgence tableau from <i>Book of the Dead</i> is a good example. All the sex, drugs, or food you could want. Why would you ever want to leave? And even beyond a lotus eater's paradise, it feels like there should be room for locations within the Hedge that are more than just pain and suffering and rage and fear and jealousy, natural places that aren't hedgesculpted by the Freehold but are still more beautiful than dangerous. For instance, a beautiful glade holding the sword of a great hero, her body transformed into a sheltering tree, with a serene, almost protective calm to the area. There's more emotions to psychoreact to than just pain. To take what someone else said &quot;on the Beautiful Madness scale, [that first section] is a bit too far on the Madness, and too short on the Beautiful parts.&quot;<br /> <br /> Other than that, I like it. I especially like the idea of changing (or gaining) a Seeming. I don't entirely see the point to such a thing, but it is certainly a nice addition, and can provide some interesting situations.<br /> <br /> I also particularly like that humans can potentially hedgesculpt, though I think it would be interesting if they could also take the Master Shaper Merit (or, perhaps they can; it's not limited to Changelings, and the Failure on warping the Hedge says that <i>most</i> humans will be unable to spend the glamour; Can humans potentially carry Glamour?)<br /> The Master Shaper Merit also seems a little underwhelming in some ways, though; at best you can create a servitor with three dots across six Attributes with one Skill dot. Not very useful when creating a book that imparts knowledge, as given in the example.<br /> <br /> I do really like that attacking Clarity uses Social Maneuvering. I really like Social Maneuvering used for other things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T21:13:48-07:00","id":973636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/973545-the-hedge-not-the-supplement-book?p=973622#post973622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That doesn't really address my complaint. There being a particular in-universe explanation for it doesn't make this any less of an un-fun feature of the game line; one that has managed to actually scare off people in my gaming group from playing Changeling, and me from wanting to use the game line.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll talk more about my take on it when I'm not juggling five things at once.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T21:29:05-07:00","id":973642,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/973545-the-hedge-not-the-supplement-book?p=973634#post973634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Master Shaper Merit also seems a little underwhelming in some ways, though; at best you can create a servitor with three dots across six Attributes with one Skill dot. Not very useful when creating a book that imparts knowledge, as given in the example..</div> </div> </div> </div>I read that very differently. It seems to me that you can spend extra glamour to give extra Attributes, with the rating of the Merit determining the rating of each Attribute. So, with Master Shaper \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 and 3 Glamour, you would be able to give Wits 3, Intelligence 3 and Composure 3 to this book, and then spend a Willpower for Academics or Occult 3.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/478-intrepid-vector","name":"Intrepid Vector","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar478_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T21:31:11-07:00","id":973643,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gullinbursti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/973545-the-hedge-not-the-supplement-book?p=973632#post973632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now feel free to educate me if I'm mistaken, but wouldn't Dreaming suit you better if you'd prefer a game more focused on the wonder of Arcadia over Lost's darker interpretation of Fae mythology? Not saying that to be snide, I don't know an excessive amount about Dreaming, but that's the impression that I get.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think, to want to play Dreaming, you need to be on as many drugs as the characters in the game.<br /> <br /> More seriously, dark doesn't have to mean miserable. Changeling is one of my favourite lines in the nWoD, coming only a short second place behind Mage, but it has some serious flaws that I am hoping 2e might correct.<br /> <br /> Changeling's big problem was always making fae magic something to run from. Any sane, sensible person bolted from it at the drop of a hat. A smart Changeling was one who did their very best to avoid magic and just kind of blended back into the mortal world. There was no incentive to go mucking with the Powers That Be and many incentives against it.<br /> <br /> That is a terrible design. When the only thing players can hope for is more misery, the game gets sad. And not in the fun way.<br /> <br /> That doesn't mean that the whole game line is bad, though. Changeling's aesthetic is fantastic; the abuse metaphor written into the creation of a Changeling and the Seasonal Courts is a delight; the direct connection to all the old folktales is wonderful.<br /> <br /> Changeling's falling-down point is incentives. It has, essentially, close to zero for engaging in the fae actions the characters are meant to, and plenty against it; a bit like how Mage 1e talked about sorcerers doing big and elaborate gestures when, in fact, the best way to do most improvised spells was to draw as little attention to yourself as possible. One of the big lessons that appeared to be learned when nWoD transitioned to CofD was that incentives <i>matter</i>, and that characters <i>and</i> players need to be incentivized (and not necessarily at the same time or in the same way).<br /> <br /> And if I'm not listened to and pain remains a central focus, well... I'll do what I've always done: Houserule the hell out of it until it's in a shape I like. Thank goodness for a versatile chassis.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/973545-the-hedge-not-the-supplement-book?p=973636#post973636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll talk more about my take on it when I'm not juggling five things at once.</div> </div> </div> </div>Take your time. I'm just killing time as I reformat a rather pathetic computer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T21:36:14-07:00","id":973646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gullinbursti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/973545-the-hedge-not-the-supplement-book?p=973612#post973612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Curious, say I create a pitchfork to fend off a scarecrow-like hobgoblin and then hightail it out of the hedge. How do you envision the decay occurring visually. Would the wood rot and metal rust away at an incredibly rapid rate, or would it revert back into bramble like vegetable material?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say it'd turn into a desiccated version of whatever it was before. If it was a metal grate before you changed it, it'd be a rusty grid of brittle metal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T21:44:06-07:00","id":973648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/973545-the-hedge-not-the-supplement-book?p=973634#post973634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not that fond of the focus on negative emotions. The Hedge should be a dangerous place, but that doesn't mean that it should make value judgements. It's psychoreactive, and that should deal with much more than just pain. I mean, this is well written, and I like the imagery, but I don't like &quot;if something doesn't hurt, the Hedge stops embodying it&quot;. There should be joy and pleasure in the Hedge (and those should be just as dangerous). I mean, to use an example you already used, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar70_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"70\" data-vbnamecard=\"70\">MachineIV</a>, The Labyrinth wasn't all horror and anguish. In fact, there was quite a lot of beauty there, and Sarah ended up in the Labyrinth in the first place because she wished for it, and got everything she asked for. I mean, there's even <a href=\"https://youtu.be/VppuD1St8Ec\" target=\"_blank\">a whole musical number</a> about how the pretty beautiful wishfulfillment is <i>more</i> dangerous than the horrors and stench bogs.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I can sort of work with that. Maybe. I'll look at what I can do there. <br /> <br /> Also, understand that not every single aspect of the setting needs to embody the full dichotomy. That's important. The Hedge isn't a half-way real, half-way Arcadia place. It's a passageway when you're escaping, and it's a passageway back. It's its own thing. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/973545-the-hedge-not-the-supplement-book?p=973634#post973634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also particularly like that humans can potentially hedgesculpt, though I think it would be interesting if they could also take the Master Shaper Merit (or, perhaps they can; it's not limited to Changelings, and the Failure on warping the Hedge says that <i>most</i> humans will be unable to spend the glamour; Can humans potentially carry Glamour?)<br /> The Master Shaper Merit also seems a little underwhelming in some ways, though; at best you can create a servitor with three dots across six Attributes with one Skill dot. Not very useful when creating a book that imparts knowledge, as given in the example.<br /> <br /> I do really like that attacking Clarity uses Social Maneuvering. I really like Social Maneuvering used for other things.</div> </div> </div> </div>Master Shaper will technically be open to human characters. I'll try to make that a little more explicitly inclusive. <br /> <br /> And Intrepid's interpretation is spot on. You could make something with 3 dots across the board if you wanted. I THINK I'm going to make it so the Skill rating is sort of &quot;seeded&quot;, where it can learn more over time. Not realistic for something you make, per se. But it seeds the possibility for things others have made, which are long-since learned.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T21:47:47-07:00","id":973649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/973545-the-hedge-not-the-supplement-book?p=973643#post973643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> More seriously, dark doesn't have to mean miserable. Changeling is one of my favourite lines in the nWoD, coming only a short second place behind Mage, but it has some serious flaws that I am hoping 2e might correct.</div> </div> </div> </div>See, I never really perceived any of this as miserable. I perceive it as risky. You have to be careful, clever, and quick, or it stings. Like I've noted, you can have perfectly normal travel in the Hedge sometimes. Just because you're in a dangerous place, doesn't mean you have to get hurt. Growing up, I lived in a tenement that is basically the model for the descriptions I used. We all had to have tetanus shots sometimes. We had to stay out of the basement most of the time because of the black mold. I lived with abusers. But we still had some great times in that house. And when I had to go down to the basement to get something, I held my breath and it was sort of exciting sometimes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T21:49:01-07:00","id":973652,"title":"","content":"Really liked the description. It reminded me very strongly of Stephen King, especially It, and that is very high praise in my books.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T21:52:30-07:00","id":973655,"title":"","content":"I'd also like to mention something completely off topic. On my computer, the topic lists this threads title as &quot;The Hedge: Not The Supplement...&quot; And my mind keeps going to Dark Knight which gives me a chuckle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5439-gullinbursti","name":"Gullinbursti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5439_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"291"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T21:58:27-07:00","id":973658,"title":"","content":"As my two cents, shouldn't Bastions and dreams at least be mentioned under the &quot;Why Changelings Delve&quot; section? Seems like a big one to skip even if it's just a page number reference to where they're discussed in depth elsewhere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10769-llegume","name":"LLegume","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T22:04:55-07:00","id":973660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LLegume</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/973545-the-hedge-not-the-supplement-book?p=973658#post973658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As my two cents, shouldn't Bastions and dreams at least be mentioned under the &quot;Why Changelings Delve&quot; section? Seems like a big one to skip even if it's just a page number reference to where they're discussed in depth elsewhere.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're probably right. That'll get added in the last pass though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T22:05:31-07:00","id":973661,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/973545-the-hedge-not-the-supplement-book?p=973652#post973652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really liked the description. It reminded me very strongly of Stephen King, especially It, and that is very high praise in my books.</div> </div> </div> </div>Needful Things is pretty much my bar for Chronicles of Darkness material. If I can hit that, I'm happy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T22:06:17-07:00","id":973663,"title":"","content":"Here's an addenda section added under &quot;Metaphysics of the Hedge&quot;. <br /> <br /> Pain and the Hedge<br /> <br /> Let\u2019s talk just a little about pain. There\u2019s a rule in the Hedge: If something stops hurting, the Hedge stops embodying it. Some read this rule to suggest that literally everything in the Hedge causes pain. That\u2019s completely false, and a simplified view of the place. It\u2019d be more appropriate to say that everything in the Hedge <i>could</i> hurt.<br /> <br /> Let\u2019s explore an example. You know that boy in high school who you really wanted to ask you out? It doesn\u2019t hurt when he finally musters the courage to ask you out. In fact, you eagerly look forward to that day. You dream about it. You run circles, practicing what you\u2019ll say to him when he finally confesses his feelings for you. Then he asks you, and your heart falls to your stomach. You cry a little the first time he holds your hand. It\u2019s beautiful and perfect and you want nothing else. The Hedge can be that. Don\u2019t you want that?<br /> <br /> But what about afterward? How does it feel when your father threatens to disown you for taking a boy home? How does it feel when he flirts with the guy who bullied you in grade school? How does it feel when he gets drunk and calls out someone else\u2019s name? How does it feel when you wake up one day and he\u2019s not there, and he\u2019s never there again? It fucking hurts. It hurts more than any spike, any thorn, any car crash. The Hedge can be that, too. What? You don\u2019t want that, too?<br /> <br /> So, the Hedge isn\u2019t all spikes and whips and rust and blood. Some of it is smokey-eyed come-hither looks. Some of it is the pie your mom made you before she died. Some of it is the feel of silk, or the weight of gold in your hand. Some of it is the childish wonder of magic made flesh, of sorcery and enchantments and quests and dragons and eternal adventure. But some of it is spikes. All of it could hurt. And if it starts hurting, it goes away once it stops hurting.<br /> <br /> Much of the time, that hurt comes from facing the reality. It\u2019s empowering to don yourself in mirror-finished platemail, charging into the cave to slay the dragon for your beloved. It\u2019s the dragon your foster mother told you about growing up. It has scales of brushed and polished platinum. It sits atop a pile of treasure, including but not limited to the lost texts of the Library of Alexandria and the magical trident held by the king of Atlantis. But at the end of that tunnel, there\u2019s a dragon, and it\u2019s very real, and its teeth are very deadly. Just because it\u2019s beautiful and wondrous doesn\u2019t mean it can\u2019t eat you alive. The Hedge can be beautiful, but make no mistake, it can eat you alive. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T22:07:56-07:00","id":973664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/973545-the-hedge-not-the-supplement-book?p=973616#post973616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because the True Fae need to fear the Hedge too, and if there is one thing they hate more than changelings can, it's pain.</div> </div> </div> </div>That really seems like a bit of a cop-out.<br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5439-gullinbursti\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5439_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5439\" data-vbnamecard=\"5439\">Gullinbursti</a> The two games are radically different, but one of the biggest problems of 1e Lost is that it focused too much on everything being DEPRESSING and TRAUMATIC. The subtitle was &quot;a game of beautiful madness&quot; and one of the four core social groups was all about the beauty and wishfulfillment of being a faerie, but the only real beauty came in the form of fancy clothes or swords made of sunlight and hoarfrost. The Hedge apparently contains no Unicorns, no fair maidens, no beautiful glades. Just razor wire thorns dripping with blood and hungry predators waiting to tear at your flesh or cheat you out of your soul.<br /> It always comes off as forced--lacking nuance, even--when every secret world is nothing but pain and sadness with no joy to be found. &quot;It's <i>Dark</i>&quot; people say. But Darkness shouldn't need to be forced. The story of Urashima Taro is already dark enough without the Dragon God's palace being filled with torture and nightmares. It's already bad enough that Beast's setting is a specific slice of the Temenos that instead of being related to strong, instinctive emotions period, might as well be known as the Darkbad, where everything is <i>FEAR</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/973545-the-hedge-not-the-supplement-book?p=973648#post973648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, understand that not every single aspect of the setting needs to embody the full dichotomy. That's important. The Hedge isn't a half-way real, half-way Arcadia place. It's a passageway when you're escaping, and it's a passageway back. It's its own thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think everything should embody the full dichotomy, but the Hedge is a place that ideally a lot of the game will take place. It's the core realm for Changelings to explore outside of social threats. It's also <i>right on the cover</i>. If anything should embody beautiful madness, it's the Hedge. To me, the Hedge in 1e was already a bit too high risk, but here any hint of it being less than an old school Gygaxian Dungeon seems thrown out the window.<br /> <br /> I mean, what happens if I hold a party in the Hedge? If I hold a ball in the Hedge? Why should it suddenly go still just because these are happy and joyous emotions instead of fear and pain? I mean, I'm not saying that it should all be a happy fun place. My first thought of &quot;that's what the Hedge is like&quot; would be the Lost Woods from the Zelda games. Sure, if you're in Kokori Village or the glade with the Master Sword it's fine and maybe even nice, but otherwise you're going to be lost forever and get that Godforsaken song stuck in your head. I can already hear it now...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And Intrepid's interpretation is spot on. </div> </div> </div>Oh. In that case it probably needs to be made clearer.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/973545-the-hedge-not-the-supplement-book?p=973663#post973663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's an addenda section added under &quot;Metaphysics of the Hedge&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's better, but it still just feels like everything has to be darkbadscaryevil. Certainly a more nuanced approach to it, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":2998,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","user":"Aspel","date":". 09-21-2016, 01:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T22:09:26-07:00","id":973665,"title":"","content":"Also, Master Shaper will allow Willpower expenditure for human characters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T22:09:55-07:00","id":973666,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/973545-the-hedge-not-the-supplement-book?p=973649#post973649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See, I never really perceived any of this as miserable. I perceive it as risky. You have to be careful, clever, and quick, or it stings. Like I've noted, you can have perfectly normal travel in the Hedge sometimes. Just because you're in a dangerous place, doesn't mean you have to get hurt. Growing up, I lived in a tenement that is basically the model for the descriptions I used. We all had to have tetanus shots sometimes. We had to stay out of the basement most of the time because of the black mold. I lived with abusers. But we still had some great times in that house. And when I had to go down to the basement to get something, I held my breath and it was sort of exciting sometimes.</div> </div> </div> </div>See, I don't get exciting out of any of that. I've danced to avoid used needles and had to hold my nose over summers because the people the next apartment over literally smeared their floors with excrement, and none of that was <i>exciting</i>. Interesting? Maybe. Definitely fun stories to tell at parties. But if someone told me &quot;Hey, wanna go live through that again?&quot;, I'd tell them to stuff it.<br /> <br /> The Hedge is defined in the preview by pain. Not (just) strong and raw emotions, but <i>pain</i>. Suffering. Agony. Misery. Nothing about it says it can be avoided; nothing suggests that pain is merely a by-product. Pain is the goal; pain is the intent; pain is the central design feature. When characters go there, the expectation is that it will hurt them in some way.<br /> <br /> That's not fun. It's something sensible people avoid. It's something that tells you every potential good thing you see is just bait in a bear trap, ready to snap shut around the arm that reaches for it.<br /> <br /> This isn't to say that pain can't or shouldn't be an integral part of the Hedge, but it does better when it's implied; when it's a natural consequence; when the very thing that can cause the pain can also be a source of reward and wonder. Just like Arcadia.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T22:14:50-07:00","id":973671,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/973545-the-hedge-not-the-supplement-book?p=973666#post973666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This isn't to say that pain can't or shouldn't be an integral part of the Hedge, but it does better when it's implied; when it's a natural consequence; when the very thing that can cause the pain can also be a source of reward and wonder. Just like Arcadia.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this is a good way of putting it. I don't need to be told that the thorns hurt, and by that same token, I don't need to be told that the memories of my dead mother's pies can hurt me. I don't need to be <i>told</i> that the denial the Spring Court indulges in can be panacea <i>and</i> poison.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T22:15:03-07:00","id":973672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/973545-the-hedge-not-the-supplement-book?p=973664#post973664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh. In that case it probably needs to be made clearer.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is current working version: <br /> <br /> New Merit: Master Shaper (\u2022, \u2022\u2022\u2022, or \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> Prerequisite: Empathy \u2022\u2022, Crafts \u2022\u2022<br /> Effect: Your character can not only imbue a semblance of sentience into an object or space in the Hedge, but can give it a spark of intelligence and independent animation. By spending a Glamour (or Willpower for a human character), she can infuse her reshaped, semi-sentient creations with a Mental or Social Attribute. This Attribute has one dot with the one-dot version of this Merit, two dots with the three-dot version of this Merit, and three dots with the five-dot version of this Merit. With a point of Willpower, she can also infuse a single Skill into an item. A single purchase of the Merit applies to all Attributes \u2013 you can give Presence \u2022\u2022 and Manipulation \u2022\u2022 to an object with Master Shaper \u2022\u2022\u2022 for instance \u2013 but each Attribute must be applied with a separate warping action.<br /> A thing with Mental and Social Attributes can react to stimuli, and can achieve limited communication depending on which Attributes it has. For example, a book with Intelligence but no Presence can impart knowledge, but might have no discernible personality. The object is still influenced greatly by the governing emotional Condition which created it.<br /> Objects with granted Skills can increase those Skills over time, with practice, communication, and teaching. This typically takes at least a year of active, part-time study per dot desired. So, for example, if a changeling wishes to teach a book Science at four dots, this would be a ten year task (the first dot coming with the Merit immediately, then two years, three, and four years). <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T22:21:10-07:00","id":973676,"title":"","content":"Just how much more time is there to playtest things, anyway? I sort of started, but then gave up because of life.<br /> Master Shaper seems like it could dovetail with Hedge Beast Companion, though.<br /> <br /> Also, are there any regular Goblins in Changeling? I only remember hobs in 1e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T22:27:23-07:00","id":973678,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/973545-the-hedge-not-the-supplement-book?p=973664#post973664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That really seems like a bit of a cop-out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, I have way too much to handle to properly answer people right now.<br /> <br /> But it's one of those design principles that's most likely to be left unaddressed, so it's worth mentioning as a hook for later on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T22:29:05-07:00","id":973679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/973545-the-hedge-not-the-supplement-book?p=973676#post973676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just how much more time is there to playtest things, anyway? I sort of started, but then gave up because of life.<br /> Master Shaper seems like it could dovetail with Hedge Beast Companion, though.<br /> <br /> Also, are there any regular Goblins in Changeling? I only remember hobs in 1e.</div> </div> </div> </div>The short answer? Not very much.<br /> <br /> The long answer? I will try to integrate stuff into the errata pass.<br /> <br /> Also, Goblins aren't NOT a thing. We're not hitting on them here. But I want to leave room to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T22:36:37-07:00","id":973681,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">This integrates a lot of the notes here. <br /> <br /> I added some description text under \u201cPain and the Hedge\u201d to add more explicit dichotomy between beautiful and dark aspects. I clarified Master Shaper to allow for human characters. I clarified some rules about warping the Hedge. I added a minor reference to Dream Bastions in the reasons changelings travel to the Hedge. I made it clear what happens to warped objects when they\u2019re taken from the Hedge into the human world.</span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=0B2K8R3qXyDyocUNHbEc0T1RQYVU\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=0B2K8R3qXyDyocUNHbEc0T1RQYVU\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=0B2K8R3qXyDyocUNHbEc0T1RQYVU\" target=\"_blank\"> https://drive.google.com/open?id=0B2K8R3qXyDyocUNHbEc0T1RQYVU </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T00:45:26-07:00","id":973709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/973545-the-hedge-not-the-supplement-book?p=973665#post973665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, Master Shaper will allow Willpower expenditure for human characters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can you please consider grouping the merit with the rest of the new merits in the book? Cross referencing one merit hidden within a separate chapter when it would be perfectly acceptable to have it with the rest of the merits (and a see &quot;new merit on page XX&quot; in Merits in the text where it would be included) is a thing I wish the CofD books would do.<br /> <br /> Having individual merits littered throughout the book is one of the most frustrating things when a game actually gets to character creation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1462,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","user":"Xenesis","date":". 09-21-2016, 04:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T01:16:01-07:00","id":973714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/973545-the-hedge-not-the-supplement-book?p=973709#post973709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Can you please consider grouping the merit with the rest of the new merits in the book? Cross referencing one merit hidden within a separate chapter when it would be perfectly acceptable to have it with the rest of the merits (and a see &quot;new merit on page XX&quot; in Merits in the text where it would be included) is a thing I wish the CofD books would do.<br /> <br /> Having individual merits littered throughout the book is one of the most frustrating things when a game actually gets to character creation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't worry about that. This was just a presentation thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T01:38:38-07:00","id":973721,"title":"","content":"Wow. From a cursory glance, this is a real improvement on 1st Edition.<br /> And it didn't even need to be improved in the first place (IMO)<br /> <br /> And, I just remembered. One of my mates made a song about the Hedge back in our Lost LARP days.<br /> <a href=\"https://soundcloud.com/klover-1/the-hedge\" target=\"_blank\">Take a listen.</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>__________________________________________________ </b><br /> <span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><b><i>Preaching the enlightened gospels of Gaming Anarchy</i></b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/225-growls","name":"Growls","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar225_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"292"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T02:20:19-07:00","id":973727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/973545-the-hedge-not-the-supplement-book?p=973593#post973593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, the Contract is a more specific rule than the Hedge section. So, it supersedes the general statement. It's a rare exception, and one that takes unique intervention. <br /> <br /> And Dream Bastions are a thing, and dream critters exist. They are in their own section dealing specifically with dreams stuff. <br /> <br /> And yes, Hedgewall should create &amp;quot;Hedge&amp;quot;, not necessarily thorns and brambles specifically. I think in the final version, I might even make it subject to warping.</div> </div> </div> </div> Making the Hedgewall subject to Hedge Warping sounds really awesome.<br /> <br /> Why I asked about the Dream Bastions is that you've been reworking Dreamwalking and I was surprised that dreams weren't on you list of reason why Lost go into the Hedge, because it seems like a really big one <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Thank you very much of answering my questions, I look forward to the book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T02:29:53-07:00","id":973729,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/973545-the-hedge-not-the-supplement-book?p=973681#post973681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">This integrates a lot of the notes here. <br /> <br /> I added some description text under \u201cPain and the Hedge\u201d to add more explicit dichotomy between beautiful and dark aspects. I clarified Master Shaper to allow for human characters. I clarified some rules about warping the Hedge. I added a minor reference to Dream Bastions in the reasons changelings travel to the Hedge. I made it clear what happens to warped objects when they\u2019re taken from the Hedge into the human world.</span></span><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=0B2K8R3qXyDyocUNHbEc0T1RQYVU\" target=\"_blank\">https://drive.google.com/open?id=0B2...UNHbEc0T1RQYVU</a></div> </div> </div> </div> Thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T03:52:07-07:00","id":973747,"title":"","content":"Can humans hedge duel?<br /> <br /> Do Fae Touched use the human or changeling rules for hollows, hedge warping, induce emotions, hedge duels?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T04:14:02-07:00","id":973748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/973545-the-hedge-not-the-supplement-book?p=973747#post973747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can humans hedge duel?</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess? I don't see why not. I don't know that it's a thing that necessarily happens. But it could happen, and it could have happened. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/973545-the-hedge-not-the-supplement-book?p=973747#post973747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do Fae Touched use the human or changeling rules for hollows, hedge warping, induce emotions, hedge duels?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm testing them with the human rules currently. I think that's probably smarter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T04:37:40-07:00","id":973753,"title":"","content":"Looking at Master Shaper merit, how does one deal with physical actions by your Hedge object, I mean say that angry flower attacks someone, how do you roll for its attacks, after all it might have been given mental/social stats, but it has no strength/dex/stamina?<br /> <br /> Also can Fae Touched use the Master Shaper merit and if so do they use it like a Changeling or Human?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T04:40:26-07:00","id":973754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/973545-the-hedge-not-the-supplement-book?p=973748#post973748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I guess? I don't see why not. I don't know that it's a thing that necessarily happens. But it could happen, and it could have happened. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I'm testing them with the human rules currently. I think that's probably smarter.</div> </div> </div> </div> Thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T04:53:51-07:00","id":973757,"title":"","content":"I think most humans that gain the Master Shaper merit would be humans who serve Changelings, Huntsmen, True Fae, more exotic fae, and so have more access. <br /> <br /> Also what do we call a creature/object that one creates by Hedge Warping, I mean its not a hobgoblin, Hedge Beast, or a Dream critter, its still apart of the hedge, not an inhabitant, and its not a Hedgespun automation. It can't leave the Hedge.<br /> <br /> Maybe Hedge Pets?<br /> <br /> Also could a specialized form of Master Shaper be the cause of Fae Mounts, because they remind me of Fae Mounts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T04:59:55-07:00","id":973761,"title":"","content":"Harmony, Satiety, Synergy I'd say should work like Clarity in the Hedge.<br /> <br /> Cover, Wisdom, Humanity, Pilgramage, Memory should work like intergity.<br /> <br /> Just my opinion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T05:56:38-07:00","id":973783,"title":"","content":"I assume that Changeling can only open a gateway from the material world, not say the Shadow, Underworld, Emination Realm?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T08:05:18-07:00","id":973857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/973545-the-hedge-not-the-supplement-book?p=973783#post973783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I assume that Changeling can only open a gateway from the material world, not say the Shadow, Underworld, Emination Realm?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Hey, what's the worst that could happen?&quot; <div align=\"center\">~ Last intelligible words of a Spring Courtier Gravewright, spoken seconds before he tries to make an Avernian Gate a Hedge Gateway.</div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 09-21-2016, 11:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T08:33:24-07:00","id":973870,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/973545-the-hedge-not-the-supplement-book?p=973857#post973857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Hey, what's the worst that could happen?&quot; <div align=\"center\">~ Last intelligible words of a Spring Courtier Gravewright, spoken seconds before he tries to make an Avernian Gate a Hedge Gateway.</div></div> </div> </div> </div> LMFAO. Even if you can't make a gateway there, I wonder if you can use the Hedgewall Contract to bring the Hedge to you in the Underworld, Shadow, Emination Realms, ect...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T09:08:44-07:00","id":973885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/973545-the-hedge-not-the-supplement-book?p=973857#post973857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&amp;quot;Hey, what's the worst that could happen?&amp;quot; <div align=\"center\">~ Last intelligible words of a Spring Courtier Gravewright, spoken seconds before he tries to make an Avernian Gate a Hedge Gateway.</div></div> </div> </div> </div>I'll second that LMFAO. <br /> <br /> Still, from the sound of things, ghosts would love the place. They're defined by beautiful things that hurt them, too-wonder if i should create a hobgoblin that is a ghost turned fae.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T09:15:17-07:00","id":973887,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2241\" data-vbnamecard=\"2241\">Omegaphallic</a> Edit your post with new thoughts instead of making a new one :V<br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8331_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8331\" data-vbnamecard=\"8331\">milo v3</a> There actually were Hedge Gateways into other realms in 1e. Including a Dead Dominion tied to Arcadia and the Hedge. Contracts of Shade and Spirit can even open an Avernian Gateway. Not to mention The Death Pact. Arcadia and it's children have had dealings with the land of the Dead before.<br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar70_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"70\" data-vbnamecard=\"70\">MachineIV</a> Promethean 2e has a little more on the Underworld, will Changeling 2e have The Death Pact in the corebook? I know there are still a few things that deal with Ghosts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":2998,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","user":"Aspel","date":". 09-21-2016, 12:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T09:50:08-07:00","id":973903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/973545-the-hedge-not-the-supplement-book?p=973666#post973666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> See, I don't get exciting out of any of that. I've danced to avoid used needles and had to hold my nose over summers because the people the next apartment over literally smeared their floors with excrement, and none of that was <i>exciting</i>. Interesting? Maybe. Definitely fun stories to tell at parties. But if someone told me &amp;quot;Hey, wanna go live through that again?&amp;quot;, I'd tell them to stuff it.<br /> <br /> The Hedge is defined in the preview by pain. Not (just) strong and raw emotions, but <i>pain</i>. Suffering. Agony. Misery. Nothing about it says it can be avoided; nothing suggests that pain is merely a by-product. Pain is the goal; pain is the intent; pain is the central design feature. When characters go there, the expectation is that it will hurt them in some way.<br /> <br /> That's not fun. It's something sensible people avoid. It's something that tells you every potential good thing you see is just bait in a bear trap, ready to snap shut around the arm that reaches for it.<br /> <br /> This isn't to say that pain can't or shouldn't be an integral part of the Hedge, but it does better when it's implied; when it's a natural consequence; when the very thing that can cause the pain can also be a source of reward and wonder. Just like Arcadia.</div> </div> </div> </div> Sometimes its worth risking pain or excepting pain. Example tomorrow I'm getting my last two wisdom teeth pulled and that will be painful, I've accepted that, but the benifits outway the discomfort of pain and swelling, improved oral health, less pain in the long term, ect...<br /> <br /> The dangerous of the Hedge are like that. Yes there is pain and risk and danger, but its worth it because you can magic fruits that give ypu glamour and heal your wounds, places were you can build a magic home/sancurary were you are safer/more powerful then anywhere else in the universe, and removing your icons from the hedge makes less pain in the long term.<br /> <br /> And I think at least for Changelings the pain can in of itself be enlighting. I assume that Changeling traveling through the thorns as opposed to trods experience breaking points over time, well suceeding on those can grant acutity condition and that can lead you gaining a point of clarity, instead of losing it.<br /> <br /> So there are lots of reasons, tons for exploring and Changeling magic, and that doesn't include how cool hedge warping really is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T10:07:38-07:00","id":973913,"title":"","content":"So according to the kiths we've been given, farwalkers reduce the level of extreme environments by their weird rating. Does this mean they can bypass the damage of the hedge as well?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5610-aslan751","name":"aslan751","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5610_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T10:52:55-07:00","id":973928,"title":"","content":"So.. Are Hobgoblins and Hobs the same thing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T11:41:00-07:00","id":973947,"title":"","content":"I think hobs are a subset of Hobgoblins, they're the most humaniod, human like ones, known for their challenging personalities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T11:44:04-07:00","id":973950,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aslan751</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/973545-the-hedge-not-the-supplement-book?p=973913#post973913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So according to the kiths we've been given, farwalkers reduce the level of extreme environments by their weird rating. Does this mean they can bypass the damage of the hedge as well?</div> </div> </div> </div> The fits them thematically, I mean it would help them walker farther through the Hedge, but I'd think that would only protect them from the extreme enviroment, not stuff like risking Clarity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T11:46:01-07:00","id":973952,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/973545-the-hedge-not-the-supplement-book?p=973885#post973885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'll second that LMFAO. <br /> <br /> Still, from the sound of things, ghosts would love the place. They're defined by beautiful things that hurt them, too-wonder if i should create a hobgoblin that is a ghost turned fae.</div> </div> </div> </div> Motion passed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T12:43:25-07:00","id":973981,"title":"","content":"This book is going to be amazing, I love you.<br /> <br /> I really need to get to GenCon at some point and desperately try to get people to sign books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T15:39:00-07:00","id":974069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/973545-the-hedge-not-the-supplement-book?p=973887#post973887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> Edit your post with new thoughts instead of making a new one :V<br /> <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> There actually were Hedge Gateways into other realms in 1e. Including a Dead Dominion tied to Arcadia and the Hedge. Contracts of Shade and Spirit can even open an Avernian Gateway. Not to mention The Death Pact. Arcadia and it's children have had dealings with the land of the Dead before.<br /> <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> Promethean 2e has a little more on the Underworld, will Changeling 2e have The Death Pact in the corebook? I know there are still a few things that deal with Ghosts.</div> </div> </div> </div> I'm sorry I missed your request. I will try and keep doubling posting to a minium, mostly if I'm qouting/responding to too different people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T15:49:32-07:00","id":974076,"title":"","content":"Also, I didn't see this until the quick revisions. I must say, I like them.<br /> <br /> Does make the opening lines kind of unfitting though-the idea is that in the Hedge, the pain is often <i>worth it. </i>Like confronting your Shadow in Persona 4; it hurts, but it can lead to a better place.<br /> <br /> Maybe pain doesn't make you stronger-but becoming stronger does often <i>involve </i>pain. Most of the good things in life do. Perhaps that is the true danger of the Hedge-it's a feral, surreal wasteland of chaos, but it's simultaneously a utopia with just enough pain to remind you it's very real. You know it's going to eat you, but it's so <i>polite </i>about eating you, so you let it gnaw.<br /> <br /> (Heh, goes to show my fanficcer side, in that what I leaped to was hurling Ace Attorney characters through the Hedge. I am honestly curious to explore what the Hedge looks like for Rayfa at the end of Spirit of Justice).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T16:31:04-07:00","id":974101,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aslan751</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/973545-the-hedge-not-the-supplement-book?p=973913#post973913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So according to the kiths we've been given, farwalkers reduce the level of extreme environments by their weird rating. Does this mean they can bypass the damage of the hedge as well?</div> </div> </div> </div>Promethean's Wasteland rules establish a precedent for particular aspects of supernatural environments bypass some forms of resistance to Extreme Environments; I'm pretty sure the Thorns can qualify.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T16:59:46-07:00","id":974118,"title":"","content":"Considering the rage of Kuruth and the pain of regeneration werewolves probably upend the place when drawn into it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T01:15:06-07:00","id":974289,"title":"","content":"I really like the link between the Hede and pain. That's probably the most evocative thing I've read about it. I'm curious about one sentence in particular: &quot;And if it<br /> starts hurting, it goes away once it stops hurting.&quot; How litteral is that? Would a rose disappear from the hedge if its thorns were removed, for example?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T02:27:02-07:00","id":974302,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/973545-the-hedge-not-the-supplement-book?p=974289#post974289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really like the link between the Hede and pain. That's probably the most evocative thing I've read about it. I'm curious about one sentence in particular: &quot;And if it<br /> starts hurting, it goes away once it stops hurting.&quot; How litteral is that? Would a rose disappear from the hedge if its thorns were removed, for example?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's relatively literal. If that's just a rose? Yes, it ceases to be once its thorns are gone. It wilts. And in its place, something else can grow. But if that rose is a specific rose which holds significance that could hurt someone still? Then it'd stick around, and regenerate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T07:54:02-07:00","id":974415,"title":"","content":"I'd still like to know &quot;Why pain?&quot;. I don't feel like that question's been answered yet. What does making pain front and centre add? What thematic space does it fill? What role does &quot;It ceases to exist if it stops hurting someone&quot; fulfill that &quot;It ceases to exist if it stops evoking the emotion it was made by&quot; not?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T09:54:24-07:00","id":974480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/973545-the-hedge-not-the-supplement-book?p=974415#post974415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd still like to know &quot;Why pain?&quot;. I don't feel like that question's been answered yet. What does making pain front and centre add? What thematic space does it fill? What role does &quot;It ceases to exist if it stops hurting someone&quot; fulfill that &quot;It ceases to exist if it stops evoking the emotion it was made by&quot; not?</div> </div> </div> </div>Now, I'm not David, or one of the writers, but I'd say its because the Hedge is not Arcadia, it is not Fairie, it is the boundary between Arcadia and Ironside. Pain is what makes it a boundary; a hedge that doesn't have an inherent drawback to traveling through it isn't much of a good barrier.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T10:00:13-07:00","id":974482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/973545-the-hedge-not-the-supplement-book?p=974415#post974415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd still like to know &quot;Why pain?&quot;. I don't feel like that question's been answered yet. What does making pain front and centre add? What thematic space does it fill? What role does &quot;It ceases to exist if it stops hurting someone&quot; fulfill that &quot;It ceases to exist if it stops evoking the emotion it was made by&quot; not?</div> </div> </div> </div>What about a place whose most pseudoconsistent feature is a massive maze-wall that tears the souls off of abductees to Arcadia and is literally called &quot;the Thorns&quot; by English-speaking changelings says anything other than &quot;pain&quot; to you?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T10:25:01-07:00","id":974499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/973545-the-hedge-not-the-supplement-book?p=974415#post974415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd still like to know &amp;quot;Why pain?&amp;quot;. I don't feel like that question's been answered yet. What does making pain front and centre add? What thematic space does it fill? What role does &amp;quot;It ceases to exist if it stops hurting someone&amp;quot; fulfill that &amp;quot;It ceases to exist if it stops evoking the emotion it was made by&amp;quot; not?</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, the revelation that the True Fae despise pain actually made it all click, for me.<br /> <br /> Pain does not help you grow it and of itself. But it does a very vital service-it tells you that something hurts. Or more importantly, that something hurts another.<br /> <br /> The Hedge is the fae world as it relates to others. Painful, yes, but also beautiful and capable of giving enlightenment beyond the rational and the conscious. To invoke a favorite anime of mine, it is a world without an AT Field, where people simply cannot run away from the feeling of themselves and others. This is both extreme boon and unforgivable curse.<br /> <br /> That's why the Keepers fear it so. The Hedge will not let you leave unless you<i> feel</i>. The Others build entire pocket universes out of their desire to <i>not feel</i>. They fear pain, and there's few worse pains than watching someone you care for be hurt, or to be reminded of your weaknesses. And that is why the Keepers can't emphasize-they really, really don't want to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","user":"Leliel","date":". 09-22-2016, 02:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T11:05:34-07:00","id":974541,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/973545-the-hedge-not-the-supplement-book?p=973665#post973665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, Master Shaper will allow Willpower expenditure for human characters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nice. Also I can't wait to see a list of Goblin fruits. That was always an interesting aspect of C:tL e1 to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7106-extant-reality","name":"Extant Reality","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7106_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"155"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T11:49:43-07:00","id":974564,"title":"","content":"I feel like my point was thoroughly missed. I am not asking for in-universe justification; I'm looking for a narrative one. What does the Hedge add to Changeling? What does it produce? What themes does it create and/or exemplify? And, in that context, what does pain serve?<br /> <br /> To me, the Hedge always existed as The Woods in fairytales; that place children are told not to wander into and do anyway, becoming lost (heh) in the process. It provides the narrative grounds whereby characters can stumble on inviting old cottages, dragon dens, dwarven mines, and such-like. I liked that aspect.<br /> <br /> 1e struggled, though, and always managed to make going into the Hedge about risk, rather than reward. It was a place you went when you had to, not when you wanted. That made all the usual fae tropes into warning signs that smart players avoided, rather than one they would be willing to risk. Granny's secretly a wolf, the dragon is not asleep, and the dwarves will make you their servant every single time. The Hedge is a place you go on sufferance, if you go at all.<br /> <br /> Making the Hedge about pain, first, foremost, always, is not learning from this mistake; it is repeating it. <br /> <br /> So I ask, because maybe there is something I am missing: Why pain? What benefit does it add that nothing else will?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T12:09:08-07:00","id":974578,"title":"","content":"As a landscaper, its not really a hedge if you don't feel pain walking through it.<br /> <br /> Narritively it forces you to confront issues,if you want the wealth of goodies you have to deal with coming across your pain, both physical and otherwise.<br /> <br /> Its part of the horror and remember as a default this is a horror story.<br /> <br /> I think in someways your encouraged to visit the hedge more in 2e, but at a massive cost, the pain and the dangers.<br /> <br /> I'm really looking forward to the core and The Hedge: the supplement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T12:24:27-07:00","id":974590,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/973545-the-hedge-not-the-supplement-book?p=974578#post974578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a landscaper, its not really a hedge if you don't feel pain walking through it.<br /> <br /> Narritively it forces you to confront issues,if you want the wealth of goodies you have to deal with coming across your pain, both physical and otherwise.<br /> <br /> Its part of the horror and remember as a default this is a horror story.<br /> <br /> I think in someways your encouraged to visit the hedge more in 2e, but at a massive cost, the pain and the dangers.<br /> <br /> I'm really looking forward to the core and The Hedge: the supplement.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except... That doesn't accord with this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/973545-the-hedge-not-the-supplement-book?p=973649#post973649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See, I never really perceived any of this as miserable. I perceive it as risky. You have to be careful, clever, and quick, or it stings. Like I've noted, you can have perfectly normal travel in the Hedge sometimes. Just because you're in a dangerous place, doesn't mean you have to get hurt.</div> </div> </div> </div>Either the Hedge forces you to confront your issues, or you can avoid them. You can't have it both ways; either the Hedge is a narrative piece designed to force you to come to terms with your pain, or it's fairyland that rewards you for <i>avoiding</i> pain. You can't have <i>both</i> in the same thing. The success condition for visiting the Hedge being getting away unscathed, laughing at that asshole goblin trying to make you into soup, is directly contrary to the idea that it serves <i>any</i> purpose in making you confront meaningful emotional hurt.<br /> <br /> You're not going into the Hedge to face your demons and overcome them; you're trying to be the lucky bugger who nicks the goblin fruit and gets out before the forest-sized venus fly trap snaps shut around you.<br /> <br /> That's really my point: We're being told the Hedge is this awesome place to go to hunt for treasures and have adventures. That doesn't accord with pain. Danger, certainly; danger absolutely makes for adventure. I think the reward angle respective to the danger can be tuned up, but danger is something I'm happy to keep.<br /> <br /> Pain isn't danger, though. Pain is... Pain. And if the Hedge lives and thrives off pain, that's what it is. It's not a dangerous place full of adventurous thrills; it is a hellscape waiting to devour you that might contain a fun trinket or two.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T12:56:57-07:00","id":974611,"title":"","content":"&quot;Pain isn't danger, though. Pain is... Pain. And if the Hedge lives and thrives off pain, that's what it is. It's not a dangerous place full of adventurous thrills; it is a hellscape waiting to devour you that might contain a fun trinket or two.&quot;<br /> <br /> Something inbetween. The potential is alot more then a trinket or two. And if its a hell scape, sometime beautiful, sometimes ugly, its one with great rewards and one that you can hammer parts of into a paradise or useful, potiently powerful things.<br /> <br /> And yeah brief exposure isn't painful, but when I said what I said I was refering to a brief jaunt down a rank 5 Trod , I refering to exploring the thorns, maybe even the dense thorns looking for things like rare goblin fruit, a powerful hob sage, searching for Icons, ect...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T13:00:53-07:00","id":974618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/973545-the-hedge-not-the-supplement-book?p=974590#post974590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Except... That doesn't accord with this:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Either the Hedge forces you to confront your issues, or you can avoid them. You can't have it both ways; either the Hedge is a narrative piece designed to force you to come to terms with your pain, or it's fairyland that rewards you for <i>avoiding</i> pain. You can't have <i>both</i> in the same thing. The success condition for visiting the Hedge being getting away unscathed, laughing at that asshole goblin trying to make you into soup, is directly contrary to the idea that it serves <i>any</i> purpose in making you confront meaningful emotional hurt.<br /> <br /> You're not going into the Hedge to face your demons and overcome them; you're trying to be the lucky bugger who nicks the goblin fruit and gets out before the forest-sized venus fly trap snaps shut around you.<br /> <br /> That's really my point: We're being told the Hedge is this awesome place to go to hunt for treasures and have adventures. That doesn't accord with pain. Danger, certainly; danger absolutely makes for adventure. I think the reward angle respective to the danger can be tuned up, but danger is something I'm happy to keep.<br /> <br /> Pain isn't danger, though. Pain is... Pain. And if the Hedge lives and thrives off pain, that's what it is. It's not a dangerous place full of adventurous thrills; it is a hellscape waiting to devour you that might contain a fun trinket or two.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think you are the one who is confusing in-universe versus out of universe aspects of the Hedge. You CAN have both of the things you mention, one is in-character, the other is game design.<br /> <br /> From a game design standpoint: The Hedge is a barrier separating Arcadia and Ironside, for both mortals and Fae. Out of character we know it does this by creating pain and &quot;forcing&quot; the character to confront that pain.<br /> <br /> In character: A changeling (or Mortal) doesn't know EXACTLY how the hedge works. They know it is dangerous, but they also have reasons to go there; not to confront their pain, but to reap those rewards. The character wants to sneak in and get away without being harmed, but that isn't what the Storyteller wants(unless you do for convience reasons, and then you do, as stated in the text).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T13:51:57-07:00","id":974644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/973545-the-hedge-not-the-supplement-book?p=974611#post974611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something inbetween. The potential is alot more then a trinket or two. And if its a hell scape, sometime beautiful, sometimes ugly, its one with great rewards and one that you can hammer parts of into a paradise or useful, potiently powerful things.<br /> <br /> And yeah brief exposure isn't painful, but when I said what I said I was refering to a brief jaunt down a rank 5 Trod , I refering to exploring the thorns, maybe even the dense thorns looking for things like rare goblin fruit, a powerful hob sage, searching for Icons, ect...</div> </div> </div> </div>What you're seeing, I don't see. If the Hedge only gives by pain, all those things are going to exact a far greater toll than they're worth and probably ultimately screw you over anyway. There's always a catch.<br /> <br /> Now, if the Hedge is, say, a <i>dangerous</i> place, rather than a painful one - one defined by story, dream logic, and all that - then we're all good because there's no requirement that the reward screw you over in some way. There's <i>promise</i> in the Hedge, and that promise is the fun part.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/973545-the-hedge-not-the-supplement-book?p=974618#post974618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you are the one who is confusing in-universe versus out of universe aspects of the Hedge. You CAN have both of the things you mention, one is in-character, the other is game design.<br /> <br /> From a game design standpoint: The Hedge is a barrier separating Arcadia and Ironside, for both mortals and Fae. Out of character we know it does this by creating pain and &quot;forcing&quot; the character to confront that pain.<br /> <br /> In character: A changeling (or Mortal) doesn't know EXACTLY how the hedge works. They know it is dangerous, but they also have reasons to go there; not to confront their pain, but to reap those rewards. The character wants to sneak in and get away without being harmed, but that isn't what the Storyteller wants(unless you do for convience reasons, and then you do, as stated in the text).</div> </div> </div> </div>Alright, I'm gonna explain myself as clearly as possible: This is a game; it is not real. It has no laws of physics that must be obeyed, no rules nor consistency that is a priori enforced. Changeling can be created and made into whatever form its writers and authors see fit. Hence, the Hedge does not need to exist, it doesn't have to be a barrier, it doesn't have to do this by creating pain.<br /> <br /> From a design standpoint, the Hedge - and any other game feature - exists for a reason; a purpose of enhancing, expanding, or otherwise improving some aspect or part of the game. The Hedge expands the play space, creates new opportunities, fills a role in the fluff.<br /> <br /> It doesn't <i>have</i> to use pain to do this. The Hedge can be justified by post hoc in the fluff any way you care to name (a contract requirement; a rule of the Old Gods; a defense by humanity against the Fae; a defense by the Fae against humanity and its iron; the aggregate of humanity's dreams and thus a place where the Gentry are not in complete control and, hence, vulnerable, etc.).<br /> <br /> So when I ask &quot;Why pain?&quot;, I am not asking for an <i>in-universe fluff justification</i>. Fluff will be what it will. I'm recognizing that someone - presumably Arcane - decided that this was something that made the Hedge <i>better</i> somehow, and I want to know why because I do not see it. What stories does this add that makes the stories it sacrifices worth it? What possibility space does it create that makes the spaces it destroys worthwhile? Why <i>this</i>, and not something else?<br /> <br /> I want an answer to that because I apparently just do not get it.<br /> <br /> And, no, you cannot have both because even if the PCs do not know what the Hedge is, their experiences with it will be coloured by its nature. If all the Hedge can ever make, ever produce, ever be is a source of pain and misery, the characters and their historical forebears will have long since come to recognize it. At the very least, it discourages the <i>players</i>, who will not want their characters to wander into a painful place full of hurt for no reason. Danger is fun, but a promise of pain? No thank you.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> I'm coming off as snappier than I'd like here and I mean nothing by it. I just want to try and make myself as plain as possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T14:15:44-07:00","id":974658,"title":"","content":"So you have your solution. If you don't like the pain part, ignore it or house rule it, problem solved for you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T14:27:22-07:00","id":974664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/973545-the-hedge-not-the-supplement-book?p=974644#post974644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And, no, you cannot have both because even if the PCs do not know what the Hedge is, their experiences with it will be coloured by its nature. If all the Hedge can ever make, ever produce, ever be is a source of pain and misery, the characters and their historical forebears will have long since come to recognize it. At the very least, it discourages the <i>players</i>, who will not want their characters to wander into a painful place full of hurt for no reason. Danger is fun, but a promise of pain? No thank you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, I think this is the disconnect.<br /> <br /> Everything the Hedge does <i>has the capacity </i>to cause pain. &quot;Can&quot; is not the same as &quot;will&quot;. As was made clear in the revisions, the pain could be the difficulties that inevitably come with true love with an actual person-it doesn't mean it <i>isn't </i>true love, it's just that life isn't a Harlequin romance. One day, no matter how much you love your partner mutually, one of you will die, and that will <i>sting. </i>But the best-case scenario has it that it will be of old age, after having lived through thick and thin together, the fire probably dulling but never ever truly fading. It can even be tangential to the actual treasures-in another example from the revisions, there's the summation of all knowledge, right there in the hoard, except oops, the very hungry and territorial dragon is guarding it, and you have to get through its very sharp and painful teeth somehow. It's only when something loses that capacity to cause pain does it vanish from the Hedge-and honestly, name five things in the world that cannot actually cause any degree of discomfort.<br /> <br /> The Hedge isn't a place of endless misery, it's a place of endless adventure-of the actual, you-may-starve-to-death-or-get-eaten-by-a-bear kind. You <i>should </i>fear it, that means you have a survival instinct. But people want adventure for a reason, there's a treasure at the end of the road. It's just a very hard road.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T14:36:05-07:00","id":974669,"title":"","content":"It occurred to be you can use the equiptment bonus you can grant stuff you can create with hedge warping, instead of physical stats for sentient Hedge Warped (okay that's the perfect name for these critters, the Hedge Warped). So for a physical actions the Hedge Warped could roll their equiptment instead of dex or strength (or stamina for anything structure or durablity doesn't work better for). You can even use the same mechanic to grant it a lethal attack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","user":"Omegaphallic","date":". 09-22-2016, 05:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T14:39:57-07:00","id":974674,"title":"","content":"Having the capacity to cause pain is not the same thing as <i>existing</i> to cause pain. There is a big difference. Stuff in the Hedge sounds like the latter.<br /> <br /> If you want the <i>capacity</i> to cause pain, any sort of danger suffices. The Hedge is the place where dreams live; a place of extremes and unreality. If you want it to be psychoactive, just let emotional extremes take hold.<br /> <br /> You get the same effect without specifically laser-sighting it on something that will drive players away.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/973545-the-hedge-not-the-supplement-book?p=974658#post974658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So you have your solution. If you don't like the pain part, ignore it or house rule it, problem solved for you.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd rather not if I don't have to, is the thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T14:56:52-07:00","id":974681,"title":"","content":"What do you want to then, I don't understand?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T15:14:58-07:00","id":974697,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/973545-the-hedge-not-the-supplement-book?p=974674#post974674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Hedge is the place where dreams live; a place of extremes and unreality.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, that's Arcadia.<br /> <br /> The Hedge is a barrier because that's why the developers included the Hedge in the first place. The Hedge exists (from an out of character, game design stand point) as a dangerous but rewarding place that connects Ironside and Arcadia. It is there to be a tempting yet very dangerous avenue to tell changeling stories in. Its painful, because this is a <b>HORROR</b> game, every positive it has should have a negative and one that on the whole leads down a more horror path. Now, why pain and not fear or anger or some other negative; that's a different question. One that has it's own answers likely to do with making it different and unique from other Otherworlds already present and covered in other ways.<br /> <br /> The Hedge was made of Thorns in 1ed too, this is not new. Just a refocusing and refining. You've already said you didnt like it then either. I think you just don't like what the Hedge is, and want it to be something else. Edit: It sounds like what you want is Arcadia without the True Fae, and that is not, nor has it ever been what the Hedge is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":1329,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","user":"ElvesofZion","date":".  Some typos and a final thought. 09-22-2016, 06:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T16:54:18-07:00","id":974747,"title":"","content":"In a place filled with pain, fear and anger are sure to follow.<br /> <br /> Only it only just dawned on me that the Hedge is like Pangaea to Arcadia's Shadow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T17:00:04-07:00","id":974751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/973545-the-hedge-not-the-supplement-book?p=974747#post974747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In a place filled with pain, fear and anger are sure to follow.<br /> <br /> Only it only just dawned on me that the Hedge is like Pangaea to Arcadia's Shadow.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, yeah, emotions aren't silos, but still picking one and focusing on it as the cause makes sense. The Shadow is predatory and alien, the Astral is also Psychoreactive but in a more universal way, except when its not, making it a place of exisitential horror, the Underworld is scary and kinda depressing, The Primordial Dream is all about fear, The Hedge is about experiencing pain and losing your way. Kinda like the rest of Changeling...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T17:34:16-07:00","id":974774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/973545-the-hedge-not-the-supplement-book?p=974674#post974674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having the capacity to cause pain is not the same thing as <i>existing</i> to cause pain. There is a big difference. Stuff in the Hedge sounds like the latter.<br /> <br /> If you want the <i>capacity</i> to cause pain, any sort of danger suffices. The Hedge is the place where dreams live; a place of extremes and unreality. If you want it to be psychoactive, just let emotional extremes take hold.<br /> <br /> You get the same effect without specifically laser-sighting it on something that will drive players away.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a sliding scale, not a binary state. Some players want no danger. Some want all danger. This is a moderately high amount of danger, with remarkable rewards that can save you from captivity. Braving the things that hurt you in order to save yourself from experiencing the worst again? To some people, that's worth it. If you're being hunted, getting your Icon could mean the difference between being caught and being free. Some will go for the goblin fruits. Some will go because Hollows are not only keen gear, but they're also potentially life-saving. Some will go because when you jump in the Hedge, the Huntsmen lose your scent. Some will go because the real world is ALSO very dangerous, and sometimes it's better to travel in the Hedge you know, rather than the jungle you don't.<br /> <br /> As a sliding scale, some players will always be driven away. From everything. It's why there aren't any games that appeal to everyone. Some players want the light-hearted approach of Toon. Some want the visceral intensity of 3:16. I cannot please every player, and trying to only leads to frustration and watered-down games. And there's a certain segment who will latch onto a specific idea, to the stark exclusion of explicitly stated content that contradicts their preconceived notions.<br /> <br /> Pretty things can hurt you. While poetic, that's true in the real world. Making that more literal in a place where abstract concepts are a little more literal? I don't think that's a big stretch.<br /> <br /> Ultimately, the Hedge isn't that much different. The rewards are higher. The idea of &quot;thorns&quot; is getting an intentionally more abstract treatment. So it sounds to me (and correct me if I'm wrong) like you just don't like the idea of the Hedge, and you want it to be something different entirely. Which is valid. But, I rather enjoy the Hedge as it is. I just wanted to make the rewards for going there a bit higher, and make the decor less assumedly uniform.<br /> <br /> And let me level with you: If I did what you were saying, I'd have dozens of people saying I was &quot;changing it for the sake of changing it&quot; and insisting that they won't touch this edition on account of that change.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":70,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","user":"MachineIV","date":". 09-22-2016, 09:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T17:44:49-07:00","id":974779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/973545-the-hedge-not-the-supplement-book?p=974751#post974751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, yeah, emotions aren't silos, but still picking one and focusing on it as the cause makes sense. The Shadow is predatory and alien, the Astral is also Psychoreactive but in a more universal way, except when its not, making it a place of exisitential horror, the Underworld is scary and kinda depressing, The Primordial Dream is all about fear, The Hedge is about experiencing pain and losing your way. Kinda like the rest of Changeling...</div> </div> </div> </div> Feel wise the Hedge feels like somewhere between the Astral and the Shadow thematically, with a touch of the Inferno in the form of thorns. Its Psycho reactive, but also more physical then the Astral, and more predatory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T17:47:04-07:00","id":974783,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/973545-the-hedge-not-the-supplement-book?p=974751#post974751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, yeah, emotions aren't silos, but still picking one and focusing on it as the cause makes sense. The Shadow is predatory and alien, the Astral is also Psychoreactive but in a more universal way, except when its not, making it a place of exisitential horror, the Underworld is scary and kinda depressing, The Primordial Dream is all about fear, The Hedge is about experiencing pain and losing your way. Kinda like the rest of Changeling...</div> </div> </div> </div> The Primordial Dream is apart of the Astral, and the Primordial Dream is all primal emotions, but Beasts only focus primarily on the one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T18:08:29-07:00","id":974792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/973545-the-hedge-not-the-supplement-book?p=974783#post974783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Primordial Dream is apart of the Astral, and the Primordial Dream is all primal emotions, but Beasts only focus primarily on the one.</div> </div> </div> </div>One is a lie, but sure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T18:30:00-07:00","id":974799,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/973545-the-hedge-not-the-supplement-book?p=974697#post974697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, that's Arcadia.<br /> <br /> The Hedge is a barrier because that's why the developers included the Hedge in the first place. The Hedge exists (from an out of character, game design stand point) as a dangerous but rewarding place that connects Ironside and Arcadia. It is there to be a tempting yet very dangerous avenue to tell changeling stories in. Its painful, because this is a <b>HORROR</b> game, every positive it has should have a negative and one that on the whole leads down a more horror path. Now, why pain and not fear or anger or some other negative; that's a different question. One that has it's own answers likely to do with making it different and unique from other Otherworlds already present and covered in other ways.<br /> <br /> The Hedge was made of Thorns in 1ed too, this is not new. Just a refocusing and refining. You've already said you didnt like it then either. I think you just don't like what the Hedge is, and want it to be something else. Edit: It sounds like what you want is Arcadia without the True Fae, and that is not, nor has it ever been what the Hedge is.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Hedge, the place where Changelings go when they dream, and where there are literal doors into the dreams of people scattered throughout it, is not the place dreams live?<br /> <br /> As for your reasoning as to why pain, I would say that my counter-point that a far better way to emphasize the horror related to Changeling is to go for extremes and not just to aim for pain innately. Aiming for pain straight and true is simplistic; it gets the job done but it only gets it done one way. Emphasizing pain first, foremost, and always removes other possibilities and dampens some of the other themes of Changeling.<br /> <br /> Consider, for example, the Seasonal Courts. The Seasonal Courts are either inspired by the Stages of Grief or they're channeling them subconsciously. All the emotions involved are in some way natural and potentially healthy but the blunt truth is that the Courts aren't <i>about</i> healthy expression; they're about compensation without moving on. Even the seemingly &quot;good&quot; Court of Spring, which supposedly spreads joy wherever it goes, is a walking pile of denial and decadence. Spring Courtiers could, theoretically, live good and noble lives in moderation and temperance but <i>the game doesn't reward that</i>. Instead, they're incentivized to be licentious and Bacchanalian revelers; drowning everyone around them in drink and drugs and decadence.<br /> <br /> That is a horror story; trying desperately to run from your past and failing; turning other people into vessels for your excess. You don't have to ruin lives, but you will, because you're an addict and the Gentry made you that way. It's a horror story <i>you</i> make because no-one forced your hand, and so you don't have the opportunity to pretend it wasn't you every step of the way when the curtain falls and the audience is applauding at the tragedy you've made of your life.<br /> <br /> The Hedge is at its best when it's the place of fairy tales; when it's the path to Grandmother's House; when it's got a dragon's lair or a cannibal's larder. A place for Changelings to indulge their fae side. The Thorns existed in 1e, but they weren't out to cause you pain; they were <i>hungry</i>. Hungry for life; for emotion; for warm blood. The Thorns were psychoactive, but the Hedge itself wasn't out innately to hurt you. It just never really had enough in it that justified the risks taken.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/973545-the-hedge-not-the-supplement-book?p=974774#post974774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is a sliding scale, not a binary state. Some players want no danger. Some want all danger. This is a moderately high amount of danger, with remarkable rewards that can save you from captivity. Braving the things that hurt you in order to save yourself from experiencing the worst again? To some people, that's worth it. If you're being hunted, getting your Icon could mean the difference between being caught and being free. Some will go for the goblin fruits. Some will go because Hollows are not only keen gear, but they're also potentially life-saving. Some will go because when you jump in the Hedge, the Huntsmen lose your scent. Some will go because the real world is ALSO very dangerous, and sometimes it's better to travel in the Hedge you know, rather than the jungle you don't.<br /> <br /> As a sliding scale, some players will always be driven away. From everything. It's why there aren't any games that appeal to everyone. Some players want the light-hearted approach of Toon. Some want the visceral intensity of 3:16. I cannot please every player, and trying to only leads to frustration and watered-down games. And there's a certain segment who will latch onto a specific idea, to the stark exclusion of explicitly stated content that contradicts their preconceived notions.<br /> <br /> Pretty things can hurt you. While poetic, that's true in the real world. Making that more literal in a place where abstract concepts are a little more literal? I don't think that's a big stretch.<br /> <br /> Ultimately, the Hedge isn't that much different. The rewards are higher. The idea of &quot;thorns&quot; is getting an intentionally more abstract treatment. So it sounds to me (and correct me if I'm wrong) like you just don't like the idea of the Hedge, and you want it to be something different entirely. Which is valid. But, I rather enjoy the Hedge as it is. I just wanted to make the rewards for going there a bit higher, and make the decor less assumedly uniform.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be perfectly honest, none of those things hold that much appeal to me.<br /> <br /> Icons are a purely reactive thing, and I've never been a huge fan of purely reactive gameplay. I've run entire games of Changeling where goblin fruit has not come up once because none of the examples from the game have been all that compelling; they seemed like the mandatory healing item, something that the Spring contracts made moot in most motleys. Hollows are neat but, again, all the benefits you're talking about are reactive; preparations the players make for a hammer coming down that, honestly, might never come.<br /> <br /> If the Hedge is all about avoiding going back to Arcadia, I'm... Honestly kind of bored with that notion. The persistent threat of the True Fae coming to get you is fun, to be sure, but it can't and shouldn't be every arc a Changeling has. The &quot;I am being hunted&quot; thing is a grand and epic peak to a story, not the main body of it; a thrilling and terrifying conclusion to an arc or even a game. It's far and away not enough meat to fuel a long-running game.<br /> <br /> I like the Hedge, but I like it as a place that lets fairytale stories play out, and that doesn't sound like where the focus is at the moment. Right now, it sounds like something that purely exists as a complication for other stories. When it's just contributing to yet more of the &quot;I want to run from everything fae&quot; side of Changeling, I feel like that's getting ignored.<br /> <br /> If no-one else agrees with me, that's fine. I'll just... Do what I did before.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T18:51:41-07:00","id":974808,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/973545-the-hedge-not-the-supplement-book?p=974799#post974799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If the Hedge is all about avoiding going back to Arcadia, I'm... Honestly kind of bored with that notion.</div> </div> </div> </div>And that's fine. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/973545-the-hedge-not-the-supplement-book?p=974799#post974799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The persistent threat of the True Fae coming to get you is fun, to be sure, but it can't and shouldn't be every arc a Changeling has.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you've gotten that impression so far, then I think there's a major disconnect going on here. I don't even think that's the only reason I've given for visiting the Hedge, let alone the myriad of other gameplay elements in play here. If anything, I've gone to painstaking efforts to provide a game where you could have other stories, when the previous edition was maybe a little too focused on that. I've literally gotten quite a bit of criticism for doing just that, and NOT hyper-focusing on that one element.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/973545-the-hedge-not-the-supplement-book?p=974799#post974799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If no-one else agrees with me, that's fine. I'll just... Do what I did before.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the base mechanics are compatible, if not identical. So, it should work pretty much the way you're used to doing it in 1E.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T18:58:54-07:00","id":974813,"title":"","content":"I think it's just kinda....the carrots of the hedge is not particularly centre stage in the writeup, while there's lots of toothy sticks showing. I mean, maybe Icons are amazingly valuable pieces of power and maybe the ability to hedgewalk is amazing, but I can definitely see where the view that the hedge is nothing but misery comes from.<br /> <br /> It's the difference between a briarpatch grown around stinging nettles and a briarpatch of blackberries in season. One just gives you cuts and stings, the other makes you brave cuts and you're rewarded with delicious fruit. (I miss blackberrying)<br /> <br /> I know from the games I've run that I've always had to amp up the wonder and awe of the hedge a lot to get players to delve, making it seem such a painful place constantly would just make my players avoid it outright.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T19:36:53-07:00","id":974822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/973545-the-hedge-not-the-supplement-book?p=974808#post974808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you've gotten that impression so far, then I think there's a major disconnect going on here. I don't even think that's the only reason I've given for visiting the Hedge, let alone the myriad of other gameplay elements in play here. If anything, I've gone to painstaking efforts to provide a game where you could have other stories, when the previous edition was maybe a little too focused on that. I've literally gotten quite a bit of criticism for doing just that, and NOT hyper-focusing on that one element.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm afraid my impression's been the opposite. Make of that what you will.<br /> <br /> For what it's worth, I do like the Huntsmen. They're just... One piece of the picture. I think if I had to ask for anything, it'd be for reasons for Changelings to want to engage in fae behaviours more. The Hedge was always a part of that because it freed them up a little. Even there, though, this problem infiltrates; the rewards for behaviours like that, last I checked, were just &quot;Huntsmen have a harder time tracking you&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/973545-the-hedge-not-the-supplement-book?p=974808#post974808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, the base mechanics are compatible, if not identical. So, it should work pretty much the way you're used to doing it in 1E.</div> </div> </div> </div>Such as it is. Can't please everyone. That said, I think Xensis said it well, really.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T19:52:09-07:00","id":974826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/973545-the-hedge-not-the-supplement-book?p=974799#post974799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the Hedge is all about avoiding going back to Arcadia, I'm... Honestly kind of bored with that notion.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm confused... did you read the section where it listed various reasons to go into the hedge, many of which had nothing to do with avoiding going back to Arcadia....?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T20:33:58-07:00","id":974846,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/973545-the-hedge-not-the-supplement-book?p=974826#post974826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm confused... did you read the section where it listed various reasons to go into the hedge, many of which had nothing to do with avoiding going back to Arcadia....?</div> </div> </div> </div>Go back, read the post in full, and see the context of what I was responding to.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T21:56:07-07:00","id":974880,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/973545-the-hedge-not-the-supplement-book?p=974846#post974846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Go back, read the post in full, and see the context of what I was responding to.</div> </div> </div> </div>I did read the post in full, I just didn't quote the entirety since I think giant quote boxes look aesthetically displeasing. &quot;If the Hedge is all about avoiding going back to Arcadia&quot; is a faulty perspective considering it's based on a single paragraph when there any many other reasons to go into the hedge listed in the doc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T02:50:55-07:00","id":974958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/973545-the-hedge-not-the-supplement-book?p=974792#post974792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One is a lie, but sure.</div> </div> </div> </div> Your right, I don't know where I got the idea that the Primordial Dream is all Primal Emotions, not just Fear, but I went back to Beast and only Fear is mentioned.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T05:08:07-07:00","id":974997,"title":"","content":"I don't think Hedge Warping can be used to create true Iron, but maybe a Fae metal with simular properties to Iron, or more exotic metals like Mithral, Admantite, and weirder still.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T05:38:58-07:00","id":975008,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/973545-the-hedge-not-the-supplement-book?p=974958#post974958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Your right, I don't know where I got the idea that the Primordial Dream is all Primal Emotions, not just Fear, but I went back to Beast and only Fear is mentioned.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is literally an entire splat called Hungers. Fear and Hunger are openly the two strongest elements.<br /> <br /> And those aside, the game does nod at the Primordial Dream in regards to other truly old emotions-Fear and Hunger may be the cornerstones as the oldest and most primal, but the other truly old emotions get some strong shadow presence for those paying attention (since everything is sex for you, I invite you to go reread all the things said about the Makara again). Everything might go back to the cornerstones in the same way everything in Changeling goes back to pain inevitably, but to suggest that Beasts and the Primordial dream are all about <i>just</i> Fear and Hunger is reductive.<br /> <br /> All this should go in another thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T06:21:58-07:00","id":975021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/973545-the-hedge-not-the-supplement-book?p=975008#post975008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is literally an entire splat called Hungers. Fear and Hunger are openly the two strongest elements.<br /> <br /> And those aside, the game does nod at the Primordial Dream in regards to other truly old emotions-Fear and Hunger may be the cornerstones as the oldest and most primal, but the other truly old emotions get some strong shadow presence for those paying attention (since everything is sex for you, I invite you to go reread all the things said about the Makara again). Everything might go back to the cornerstones in the same way everything in Changeling goes back to pain inevitably, but to suggest that Beasts and the Primordial dream are all about <i>just</i> Fear and Hunger is reductive.<br /> <br /> All this should go in another thread.</div> </div> </div> </div> Not really thing is sex for me, there is also my fears, hunger, sleep, laugher, my love of Science Fiction/Fantasy/Horror, my wish for a better world and world peace for all.<br /> <br /> But yeah my libdo is a big part of me, I have the libdo of a man half my age, and the vivid imagination to explore it in safe ways. Maybe that's partly why Beast and Changeling are the game lines resenate with me the most.<br /> <br /> And in fact I do remember having experiences as a child in water that were very Makara in nature, so Makara is the easiest of the Beasts for me to connect too.<br /> <br /> Anyways","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","user":"Omegaphallic","date":". 09-23-2016, 09:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T06:27:32-07:00","id":975025,"title":"","content":"Anyway moving on, it occurs to me that a Mortal with the Master Shaper merit and/or Hollow would qualify for the Supernal Tolerence merit from Hurt Locker.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T08:45:41-07:00","id":975075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/973545-the-hedge-not-the-supplement-book?p=974997#post974997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think Hedge Warping can be used to create true Iron, but maybe a Fae metal with simular properties to Iron, or more exotic metals like Mithral, Admantite, and weirder still.</div> </div> </div> </div>That'll be clarified in other parts. Basically the iron section.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T08:46:14-07:00","id":975076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/973545-the-hedge-not-the-supplement-book?p=975025#post975025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway moving on, it occurs to me that a Mortal with the Master Shaper merit and/or Hollow would qualify for the Supernal Tolerence merit from Hurt Locker.</div> </div> </div> </div>Absolutely it would. I'd LOVE to do a Merit Template like we did in Hurt Locker, for human shapers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T09:56:16-07:00","id":975103,"title":"","content":"That would be awesome. It sounds like it would fit thematically into The Hedge source book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T17:24:29-07:00","id":975295,"title":"","content":"So, I'm a little late to the party, but I LOVE this!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T17:47:58-07:00","id":975307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/973545-the-hedge-not-the-supplement-book?p=975076#post975076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Absolutely it would. I'd LOVE to do a Merit Template like we did in Hurt Locker, for human shapers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Funnily enough, we are doing a supplement that could probably have a place for that.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T19:08:08-07:00","id":975331,"title":"","content":"I think my favorite bit is actually where it talks about Arcadia's laws being like the warping effects of the hedge amped up to 11. I really like the idea that &quot;Arcadia&quot; might just be the effect the Gentry have on the Hedge, and a Keeper's realm might just be the True Fae equivalent of a Hollow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T21:42:26-07:00","id":975371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/973545-the-hedge-not-the-supplement-book?p=975331#post975331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think my favorite bit is actually where it talks about Arcadia's laws being like the warping effects of the hedge amped up to 11. I really like the idea that &quot;Arcadia&quot; might just be the effect the Gentry have on the Hedge, and a Keeper's realm might just be the True Fae equivalent of a Hollow.</div> </div> </div> </div>I never really say this, but I feel like the Hedge is sort of what happens when both worlds bleed into each other. Neither way works right. Both ways resist each other, which is uncomfortable and often disastrous, but also can make magnificent procedural art. It's like when a hardcore introvert artist hooks up with a super extrovert planner. It's usually a bad idea. But the cool things that can come out of it are remarkable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T06:12:58-07:00","id":975484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/973545-the-hedge-not-the-supplement-book?p=975371#post975371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I never really say this, but I feel like the Hedge is sort of what happens when both worlds bleed into each other. Neither way works right. Both ways resist each other, which is uncomfortable and often disastrous, but also can make magnificent procedural art. It's like when a hardcore introvert artist hooks up with a super extrovert planner. It's usually a bad idea. But the cool things that can come out of it are remarkable.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's an interesting concept.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5610-aslan751","name":"aslan751","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5610_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T11:24:38-07:00","id":975614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/973545-the-hedge-not-the-supplement-book?p=975371#post975371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I never really say this, but I feel like the Hedge is sort of what happens when both worlds bleed into each other. Neither way works right. Both ways resist each other, which is uncomfortable and often disastrous, but also can make magnificent procedural art. It's like when a hardcore introvert artist hooks up with a super extrovert planner. It's usually a bad idea. But the cool things that can come out of it are remarkable.</div> </div> </div> </div>Did someone say &quot;procedural&quot;? I am surprised that no one has ever done a survival game based on the Hedge or in that case &quot;Horror-survival&quot;. Also has anyone ever seen No Man's Sky? It reminds me greatly of the randomness one might find in the Hedge. Seriously though, some kind of horror-survival campaign seems more viable now. Life is pain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7106-extant-reality","name":"Extant Reality","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7106_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"155"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T18:02:21-07:00","id":975748,"title":"","content":"It occurs to me that someone with Master Shaper and the Hollow Merits, could craft a sentient hollow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T19:06:49-07:00","id":975763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/973545-the-hedge-not-the-supplement-book?p=975748#post975748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It occurs to me that someone with Master Shaper and the Hollow Merits, could craft a sentient hollow.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a thing I want to do more with in The Hedge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T03:11:56-07:00","id":975900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/973545-the-hedge-not-the-supplement-book?p=975763#post975763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is a thing I want to do more with in The Hedge.</div> </div> </div> </div> Awesome, I look forward to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T12:22:36-07:00","id":976657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Extant Reality</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/973545-the-hedge-not-the-supplement-book?p=975614#post975614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did someone say &quot;procedural&quot;? I am surprised that no one has ever done a survival game based on the Hedge or in that case &quot;Horror-survival&quot;. Also has anyone ever seen No Man's Sky? It reminds me greatly of the randomness one might find in the Hedge. Seriously though, some kind of horror-survival campaign seems more viable now. Life is pain.</div> </div> </div> </div>Videogames are decent at telling you how to feel, but designers have yet to figure out how to understand how you (or your character) feel and react to that usefully.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T13:33:31-07:00","id":976704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/973545-the-hedge-not-the-supplement-book?p=974799#post974799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Hedge is at its best when it's the place of fairy tales; when it's the path to Grandmother's House; when it's got a dragon's lair or a cannibal's larder. A place for Changelings to indulge their fae side. The Thorns existed in 1e, but they weren't out to cause you pain; they were <i>hungry</i>. Hungry for life; for emotion; for warm blood. The Thorns were psychoactive, but the Hedge itself wasn't out innately to hurt you. It just never really had enough in it that justified the risks taken.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> I like the Hedge, but I like it as a place that lets fairytale stories play out, and that doesn't sound like where the focus is at the moment. Right now, it sounds like something that purely exists as a complication for other stories. When it's just contributing to yet more of the &quot;I want to run from everything fae&quot; side of Changeling, I feel like that's getting ignored.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry for resurrecting this sub-thread when you seem pretty done with it, but I wanted to weigh in and I've been out of town.<br /> <br /> As I read it, the Hedge isn't innately out to hurt you. It's not about harming travelers; it's about <i>expressing pain</i>. And pain, when expressed, is empathized with, and that empathy induces your own pain. That's the general case: in the specific case, of course, it's expressing <i>your</i> pain so it doesn't work like that at all. Changelings, more than any other splat, weaponize emotion and empathy, which gives them an understanding of those things that exceed an average human's... and that understanding comes in the form of losing Clarity. They get it, and in getting it, are hurt by it.<br /> <br /> Someone who's genuinely innocent or ignorant, I think, will have little trouble navigating the Hedge. It would be frightening, but it wouldn't hurt you and once you're through it, you wouldn't have a problem letting go of what you just went through. So someone like Little Red Riding Hood has no real struggle. The wolf will walk out of the brambles and ask her plans and will slink away with her answers. The loss of her innocence happens <i>later</i>, after she's left the Hedge, at Grandmother's House. But no one's <i>really</i> that innocent or ignorant. You've heard things. Things that you don't really understand, perhaps, but you've imagined what they might be. And the Hedge would take those imaginations and magnify them into terrifying realities: thorns that are then capable of shredding your Integrity.<br /> <br /> Fundamentally, I don't think that has anything to do with running from the Gentry. The Gentry aren't terribly impressed by the Hedge, if you read the spoiler again. Sure, they might fear it, but they aren't harmed by it because they're incapable of empathy. You don't go into the Hedge to run <i>away</i> from Arcadia; you go in when you've accepted that Arcadia is part of you. In a sense, the Hedge can be empowering as the realm that expresses the Gentry's unwillingness to go Ironside.<br /> <br /> But circling back away from the fluff-based justifications, I would point this out: you can play out fairy tales anywhere. If that's the value of the Hedge, then the Hedge has no value. It is, as noted, simply the Woods on the edge of town, just on the other side of the river, where the outcasts live in their secret forest kingdom. Instead, I would point at the statement (I think Arcane made it? But I can't find it in the thread again) that everything about Changelings ultimately comes back to pain. The Hedge isn't a garrison against the Gentry; it's the one place that fully manifests the themes of Changeling.<br /> <br /> The Hedge is a borderland you don't cross, because you want to never go back. It's safer at home.<br /> The Hedge is the stripping away of your mask, that pretense you put up saying that you didn't go through a Durance.<br /> The Hedge is about brutal honesty. You come out transformed because it won't let you deny truths.<br /> The Hedge is about dreams: hopes and fears and secret feelings. It's always there, that excuse and wish to explore beyond the border.<br /> <br /> And all of it hurts. Because what a fairy tale really is? Is about growing pains.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T21:24:12-07:00","id":976935,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure I ever quite put it in those words, but yes. If you strip Changeling the Lost down to a word, that word is pain.<br /> <br /> And really, that entire post of yours, Errol, is a fantastic case of <i>getting it</i>. Pat yourself on the back.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T22:18:17-07:00","id":976967,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/973545-the-hedge-not-the-supplement-book?p=976704#post976704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry for resurrecting this sub-thread when you seem pretty done with it, but I wanted to weigh in and I've been out of town.<br /> <br /> As I read it, the Hedge isn't innately out to hurt you. It's not about harming travelers; it's about <i>expressing pain</i>. And pain, when expressed, is empathized with, and that empathy induces your own pain. That's the general case: in the specific case, of course, it's expressing <i>your</i> pain so it doesn't work like that at all. Changelings, more than any other splat, weaponize emotion and empathy, which gives them an understanding of those things that exceed an average human's... and that understanding comes in the form of losing Clarity. They get it, and in getting it, are hurt by it.<br /> <br /> Someone who's genuinely innocent or ignorant, I think, will have little trouble navigating the Hedge. It would be frightening, but it wouldn't hurt you and once you're through it, you wouldn't have a problem letting go of what you just went through. So someone like Little Red Riding Hood has no real struggle. The wolf will walk out of the brambles and ask her plans and will slink away with her answers. The loss of her innocence happens <i>later</i>, after she's left the Hedge, at Grandmother's House. But no one's <i>really</i> that innocent or ignorant. You've heard things. Things that you don't really understand, perhaps, but you've imagined what they might be. And the Hedge would take those imaginations and magnify them into terrifying realities: thorns that are then capable of shredding your Integrity.<br /> <br /> Fundamentally, I don't think that has anything to do with running from the Gentry. The Gentry aren't terribly impressed by the Hedge, if you read the spoiler again. Sure, they might fear it, but they aren't harmed by it because they're incapable of empathy. You don't go into the Hedge to run <i>away</i> from Arcadia; you go in when you've accepted that Arcadia is part of you. In a sense, the Hedge can be empowering as the realm that expresses the Gentry's unwillingness to go Ironside.<br /> <br /> But circling back away from the fluff-based justifications, I would point this out: you can play out fairy tales anywhere. If that's the value of the Hedge, then the Hedge has no value. It is, as noted, simply the Woods on the edge of town, just on the other side of the river, where the outcasts live in their secret forest kingdom. Instead, I would point at the statement (I think Arcane made it? But I can't find it in the thread again) that everything about Changelings ultimately comes back to pain. The Hedge isn't a garrison against the Gentry; it's the one place that fully manifests the themes of Changeling.<br /> <br /> The Hedge is a borderland you don't cross, because you want to never go back. It's safer at home.<br /> The Hedge is the stripping away of your mask, that pretense you put up saying that you didn't go through a Durance.<br /> The Hedge is about brutal honesty. You come out transformed because it won't let you deny truths.<br /> The Hedge is about dreams: hopes and fears and secret feelings. It's always there, that excuse and wish to explore beyond the border.<br /> <br /> And all of it hurts. Because what a fairy tale really is? Is about growing pains.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, this is really phenomenal stuff. I dig.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T04:18:01-07:00","id":977108,"title":"","content":"I really, really like the new write up. The writing is more tightly focused and the mechanics are so much cleaner than first edition. I do see the concern on some players being turned away by the predominant focus on how the place can hurt you, which is a tough balancing act, because the Hedge should be scary. Characters should have reasons to be hesitant about going there. At the same time, they should also have reasons to face that fear, to decide the gain is worth the risk. In terms of actual mechanics I don't think the Hedge is nearly as bad as some people are reading it to be. Even wandering around off the trods in most cases you're taking one bashing per hour, and you can mitigate that by traveling more slowly. Or shape a temporary hollow and rest for an hour before pushing on. That just doesn't say &quot;never do this&quot; to me. Some of my best adventures have involved bruises and bloody knuckles and blistered feet. Hell, I work outside and I'm constantly getting nicks and scrapes, and sure they sting for a couple minutes but that doesn't stop me from enjoying the work. At the end of it you come home, and the scratches heal and fade away, or they become scars that you tell stories about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T21:06:59-07:00","id":977584,"title":"","content":"Oh, and for those curious, this is the short version in the &quot;high concept&quot; introduction section talking in simple terms about game concepts.<br /> <br /> The Hedge<br /> <br /> \u201cAs soon as there is life, there is danger.\u201d<br /> \u2015 Ralph Waldo Emerson<br /> <br /> Of course, the Hedge was a place every changeling passed through on the way out of Arcadia. It's a place where every changeling left something behind, a piece of themselves torn asunder by the thorns. But after the escape, the Hedge takes on a whole new role in changeling life. <br /> <br /> The Hedge is a dangerous place. Its thorns, its paths, they bend and twist and decay and grow anew at a moment's notice. Off established roads, called trods, the path is a savage garden, a vicious and frustrating jungle. Why would anyone ever return?<br /> <br /> The Hedge offers just as many rewards as dangers. Mysterious goblin fruits grow on the Hedge's plantlife, fruits which are Glamour welled up and calcified, easily consumable and offering sometimes miraculous advantages to their consumers. The Hedge offers a remarkably savvy way to elude the True Fae and the Huntsmen, after all, the Hedge is a dangerous and confusing path even for the fae. Also, many changelings carve out safe places within the Hedge, these &quot;hollows&quot; are free of prying eyes and hunting hearts. Also, changelings can walk in and manipulate dreams, and they usually do this by entering an individual's dreams through portals found deep in the Hedge. <br /> <br /> The Hedge is a psychoreactive place; it bends, contorts, and reshapes to personify emotions and fears. Of course, this is jarring to everyone the first time, and perhaps even the hundredth time. But, it's also amazing and truly awesome when wielded expertly. Imagine your curiosity the first time you heard of 3d printing technology. The Hedge is all that to the Nth degree \u2015 if you can imagine it, the Hedge can become it. The Hedge doesn't care about petty laws of physics. In the Hedge, you're as powerful as you are creative. Your strength in the Hedge equates to your strength of passion and will. So to the Lost, the Hedge can be just as empowering as it is dangerous.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T04:35:29-07:00","id":977686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/973545-the-hedge-not-the-supplement-book?p=977584#post977584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, and for those curious, this is the short version in the &amp;quot;high concept&amp;quot; introduction section talking in simple terms about game concepts.<br /> <br /> The Hedge<br /> <br /> \u201cAs soon as there is life, there is danger.\u201d<br /> \u2015 Ralph Waldo Emerson<br /> <br /> Of course, the Hedge was a place every changeling passed through on the way out of Arcadia. It's a place where every changeling left something behind, a piece of themselves torn asunder by the thorns. But after the escape, the Hedge takes on a whole new role in changeling life. <br /> <br /> The Hedge is a dangerous place. Its thorns, its paths, they bend and twist and decay and grow anew at a moment's notice. Off established roads, called trods, the path is a savage garden, a vicious and frustrating jungle. Why would anyone ever return?<br /> <br /> The Hedge offers just as many rewards as dangers. Mysterious goblin fruits grow on the Hedge's plantlife, fruits which are Glamour welled up and calcified, easily consumable and offering sometimes miraculous advantages to their consumers. The Hedge offers a remarkably savvy way to elude the True Fae and the Huntsmen, after all, the Hedge is a dangerous and confusing path even for the fae. Also, many changelings carve out safe places within the Hedge, these &amp;quot;hollows&amp;quot; are free of prying eyes and hunting hearts. Also, changelings can walk in and manipulate dreams, and they usually do this by entering an individual's dreams through portals found deep in the Hedge. <br /> <br /> The Hedge is a psychoreactive place; it bends, contorts, and reshapes to personify emotions and fears. Of course, this is jarring to everyone the first time, and perhaps even the hundredth time. But, it's also amazing and truly awesome when wielded expertly. Imagine your curiosity the first time you heard of 3d printing technology. The Hedge is all that to the Nth degree \u2015 if you can imagine it, the Hedge can become it. The Hedge doesn't care about petty laws of physics. In the Hedge, you're as powerful as you are creative. Your strength in the Hedge equates to your strength of passion and will. So to the Lost, the Hedge can be just as empowering as it is dangerous.</div> </div> </div> </div> I like it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T13:18:09-07:00","id":978566,"title":"","content":"so, I was hearing <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4Wci0l_wCOw\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> song, and it immediately made me think about &quot;being lost in the Hedge&quot; as it is portrayed in the new edition, and I've thought I should share it :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T07:49:08-07:00","id":982689,"title":"","content":"Vague thought on Hollows: The Hedge is basically congealed emotion and (mental) issues, right? Or something very psycho-reactive. Hedge-shaping is imposing your will upon it to mold and stabilize the exact form it takes, yes? Since Hollows are &quot;permanent&quot; islands of stability in the Hedge, even without a will holding them in place, shouldn't they need some other thing or property to give anchor for their stability? Maybe each Hollow could, at their core, be based around a story/trait/role - they embody that thing, which gives them permanence in the Hedge as long as they are that thing.<br /> <br /> Sorry for the thought-stream. I'm not sure what mechanical impact any of this would potentially have. Just a &quot;Tree House&quot; Hollow isn't just that, but rather the embodiment of the &quot;Hidden Tree House in the Glade&quot;. Each Hollow having its own story.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T12:34:02-07:00","id":982853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/973545-the-hedge-not-the-supplement-book?p=982689#post982689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since Hollows are &quot;permanent&quot; islands of stability in the Hedge, even without a will holding them in place, shouldn't they need some other thing or property to give anchor for their stability? Maybe each Hollow could, at their core, be based around a story/trait/role - they embody that thing, which gives them permanence in the Hedge as long as they are that thing.<br /> <br /> Sorry for the thought-stream. I'm not sure what mechanical impact any of this would potentially have. Just a &quot;Tree House&quot; Hollow isn't just that, but rather the embodiment of the &quot;Hidden Tree House in the Glade&quot;. Each Hollow having its own story.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would suggest &quot;memory&quot;. Let's say a Hollow is essentially how a particular Hedgeshaper remembers a story, or an event, or whatnot. In dreams, memories tend to be hodgepodge props that are kludged together to serve as a setting for how it's playing out. I could see fun things like echoes of voices from a domestic argument belonging to no one, or the persistent smell of cumin even though the cupboard is bare, showing up in a Hollow simply as sense-memories that refuse to be forgotten as part of the Hollow.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't bother with a mechanical impact, but if you really wanted one, I'd look at giving an environmental bonus of the same scale as a Kith Blessing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T11:04:03-07:00","id":983410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/973545-the-hedge-not-the-supplement-book?p=982853#post982853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would suggest &quot;memory&quot;. Let's say a Hollow is essentially how a particular Hedgeshaper remembers a story, or an event, or whatnot. In dreams, memories tend to be hodgepodge props that are kludged together to serve as a setting for how it's playing out. I could see fun things like echoes of voices from a domestic argument belonging to no one, or the persistent smell of cumin even though the cupboard is bare, showing up in a Hollow simply as sense-memories that refuse to be forgotten as part of the Hollow.</div> </div> </div> </div>It would be really neat if you needed to anchor a Hollow with a memory or a dream. It adds a cool irony that the process of making a safe place requires you making yourself vulnerable by putting something intimate to you out there. Anyone with access to your Hollow is kind of inside your head and can discover things about you by being perceptive or poking around. I kind of think of it like when Ariadne gets into Dom's dream in Inception. It's a series of memory vignettes connected like floors of a building by an elevator, each one a place of deep emotional importance to him.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Re-reading the draft of the dreaming rules, it would make sense that Hollows start out as Bastions that you reinforce to keep them from disappearing when you wake up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Eric Christian Berg</b><br /> <i>Onyx Path Freelancer</i><br /> Promethean: The Created Second Edition, Dark Eras Companion","edited":{"userid":2019,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2019-eberg","user":"eberg","date":". 10-07-2016, 02:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2019-eberg","name":"eberg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2019_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"284"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T18:08:45-07:00","id":985832,"title":"","content":"I just occurred to me what a hedge duel with a Cambion would be like. You attack it with the hedge, it eats that part, you try and make a monster out of the hedge, it eats that too, you make weapon of the hedge, which Cambion eats, you say fuck it, and try a contract, nope, its absorbs that Glamour too. Finally fed up with the stalemate, you say fuck it and offer to buy the Cambion a beer and talk things out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}